    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17200": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner (Part-TIme, up to 19 hours)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Nurse Practitioner (Part-TIme, up to 19 hours) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Nurse Practitioner (Part-TIme, up to 19 hours) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02235 Job Title Nurse Practitioner (Part-TIme, up to 19 hours) Position Number IP-1 (Internal Payroll) FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union No Response Pay Grade Level Grade: N/A Pay Grade Range $70hr (part-time hourly rate) Status Academic Year, Permanent, Part-time Department Information Department Medical Services Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Position is part-time (up to 19-hours per week) academic year Job Description Summary About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. _________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide independent clinical care, assessing, diagnosing, and managing acute and chronic conditions within the scope of Student Health Services and Rhode Island General Laws, Chapter 5-34, in collaboration with other licensed health care professionals. Duties and Responsibilities ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform comprehensive physical examinations and develop holistic care plans. Diagnose and treat acute and chronic conditions, independently prescribing and administering medications and therapeutics within written protocol. Maintain accurate, auditable clinical records. Refer patients to specialists and conduct follow-up. Consult and collaborate with physicians, particularly on complex cases, and initiate emergency treatment as needed. Participate in developing clinical protocols, quality improvement, and peer review. Provide health promotion and wellness counseling. SCHEDULE AND STATUS : This is a part-time, non-benefited position of up to 19 hours per week. The Medical Director sets days and hours based on clinical coverage needs. A non-standard work week may be required. LICENSES AND CERTIFICATIONS : Current Rhode Island Registered Nurse license; Rhode Island Registered Nurse Practitioner license with prescriptive privileges; Federal DEA registration; and CPR certification. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Master’s degree in nursing and a bachelor’s degree in nursing or a related field from an accredited institution. 2. Current licenses and certifications as listed above. 3. Two years of experience as a nurse practitioner in family practice or adult medicine, or completion of the URI Student Health Services fellowship. 4. Demonstrated clinical skill to practice without direct supervision, including documented experience with routine outpatient GYN care. 5. Demonstrated experience with Electronic Health Records ( EHR ). 6. Demonstrated strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. 7. Ability to work with diverse groups and coordinate support staff. 8. Ability to prepare reports and make recommendations. 9. Ability to work the assigned schedule, including a non-standard week if required. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience with college health and behavioral health care. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO STATEMENT : URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request a reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/10/2026 Closing Date 10/24/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17183 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
