    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17053": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, RI NSF EPSCoR (Experimental Program to Stimulate Competitive Research)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, RI NSF EPSCoR (Experimental Program to Stimulate Competitive Research) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Director, RI NSF EPSCoR (Experimental Program to Stimulate Competitive Research) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02205 Job Title Assistant Director, RI NSF EPSCoR (Experimental Program to Stimulate Competitive Research) Position Number PS#00008188 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 12 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $90,000 - $95,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Research Office Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes Position is full-time calendar year, limited to 06/26/2027 with possible extension. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by October 2, 2026. Applications received after October 2, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide strategic, operational, and administrative leadership for Rhode Island’s NSF EPSCoR Cooperative Agreement “Rhode Island Network for Excellence in Science and Technology”, which oversees the jurisdictional EPSCoR office. The Assistant Director is responsible for overseeing program management, financial operations, reporting, compliance, and multi-institutional coordination. This role ensures alignment with NSF priorities and project goals while supporting the Project Director in advancing statewide research capacity and workforce development. This position elevates beyond project coordination to include program leadership, decision-making authority, and external representation of EPSCoR initiatives. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Program Leadership & Strategy Partner with the Project Director/PI to plan, implement, and assess progress towards project goals and long-term strategy. Provide leadership across all research infrastructure cores, ensuring alignment with NSF EPSCoR objectives and statewide research priorities. Represent EPSCoR in institutional, regional, and national meetings and collaborations. Financial & Operational Oversight Provide oversight of all financial operations, including budget development, projections, and monitoring across all program implementation components and subawards. Ensure fiscal integrity and compliance with NSF , federal Uniform Guidance, and institutional policies. Oversee subrecipient management, invoicing, and financial reporting processes. Approve and monitor expenditures, budget reallocations, and financial planning activities. Supervise logistics and execution of major EPSCoR activities, including site visits, annual meetings, and research conferences. Research Administration & Compliance Ensure compliance with NSF policies, reporting requirements, and cooperative agreement terms. Support the PI in establishing and maintaining relationships with NSF Program Officers and grants management staff. Oversee preparation and submission of annual reports, proposals, site visit materials, and renewal applications. Maintain awareness of evolving federal regulations and ensure communication and implementation across EPSCoR stakeholders. Data Management & Evaluation Direct program-wide data collection, management, analysis, and reporting processes. Oversee evaluation activities, including coordinating with the external evaluation team and conducting internal tracking of performance metrics Ensure data systems and reporting tools meet NSF requirements and support decision-making. Partnership & Stakeholder Engagement Serve as senior liaison for partner institutions, including research administrators, faculty, and external collaborators. Strengthen statewide and regional partnerships to expand research capacity and funding competitiveness. Identify and pursue new collaborations and funding opportunities. Supervision & Team Leadership Supervise and mentor program staff, including graduate students and administrative personnel. Establish performance expectations, provide professional development, and ensure effective team operations. Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-performing team environment. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Act on behalf of the Project Director as needed in programmatic and administrative matters. Lead special projects and strategic initiatives. Perform additional duties as required to support the EPSCoR mission. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers; enterprise systems; data management platforms; Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word, etc.); grant management systems. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Master’s degree in business administration, public administration, science administration, or other relevant field (or Bachelor’s with significant equivalent experience). Minimum of 5–7 years of progressively responsible experience in research administration, program management, or federally funded programs. Demonstrated leadership experience managing complex, multi-institutional programs. Strong financial management experience, including budgeting, forecasting, and compliance oversight. Demonstrated knowledge of federal grant regulations (e.g., NSF or NIH ). Proven ability to manage multiple priorities and lead strategic initiatives. Excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse stakeholders across institutions. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : Experience managing NSF EPSCoR or similar large cooperative agreements. Experience with program evaluation, data systems, and performance metrics. Familiarity with research capacity-building programs and STEM workforce development initiatives. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Travel within and outside Rhode Island is required. Posting Date 09/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17040 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree in business administration, public administration, science administration, or other relevant field (or Bachelor’s with significant equivalent experience)? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of 5–7 years of progressively responsible experience in research administration, program management, or federally funded programs? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated leadership experience managing complex, multi-institutional programs? Yes No * Do you have strong financial management experience, including budgeting, forecasting, and compliance oversight? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge of federal grant regulations (e.g., NSF or NIH)? Yes No * Do you have proven ability to manage multiple priorities and lead strategic initiatives? Yes No * Do you have excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse stakeholders across institutions? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
