    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16870": {
      "title": "Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, College of Health Sciences",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, College of Health Sciences Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, College of Health Sciences Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Diversity Statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02184 Job Title Associate Dean for Academic and Faculty Affairs, College of Health Sciences Position Number 108234 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 18 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $175,000 - $195,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean Health Sciences Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes This is a 12-month full-time (including administrative, research and teaching) position with three-year renewable term. _______________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 23, 2026. Applications received after August 23, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The College of Health Sciences includes seven departments (Communicative Disorders, Human Development and Family Science, Kinesiology, Nutrition, Physical Therapy, Psychology, and Public Health), as well as the Interdisciplinary Neuroscience Program, the Osher Lifelong Learning Institute, and the Program in Gerontology. The College offers seven undergraduate degrees with a total enrollment of 2,460 students. The College offers eight master’s degree programs and four doctoral degree programs with a total graduate enrollment of 264 graduate students. There are 90 faculty members in the college. The College operates five on campus clinics and two off campus clinics, as well as two child development centers. POSITION SUMMARY : Provide strategic leadership as a key member of the College’s Administrative Leadership Team, overseeing all aspects of academic programs and faculty affairs in partnership with the Dean. Work collaboratively with college leadership to support alignment of academic priorities, resources, and operations. Champion faculty excellence through mentorship and transparent management of career milestone processes, while driving innovation in curriculum design, program quality, and program promotion that advances the College’s mission and impact in health sciences education and scholarship. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Academic Program Leadership & Excellence Provide strategic leadership for the College’s undergraduate and graduate programs, championing innovation in curriculum design, program promotion, program assessment, accreditation and quality improvement that advances student success and prepares graduates for evolving professional landscapes. Lead and mentor undergraduate and graduate program directors, fostering a collaborative community of practice focused on pedagogical excellence and continuous improvement. Partner strategically with the Assistant Dean for Student Affairs to create seamless, student-centered experiences in advising, enrollment management, and holistic student support. Faculty Affairs & Professional Development Serve as Senior Leader, alongside the Dean, of all faculty affairs processes—including recruitment, retention, review, tenure, and promotion—ensuring equity, transparency, and alignment with the College’s mission and values. Champion faculty success by providing expert guidance and mentorship to faculty and department chairs throughout career milestones, interpreting University policies, collective bargaining agreements, and best practices with clarity and care. Collaborate with the Dean, Department Chairs and other university entities to manage faculty and/or student conflicts, address policy and worload concerns, and promote a collegial, supportive, and invlusie institutional culture. Cultivate a thriving academic culture that values diversity, innovation, and scholarly excellence across all disciplines within the College. Governance & Advisory Leadership Serve as a trusted advisor and thought partner to the Dean on all academic and faculty matters, bringing data-informed insights, creative problem-solving, and institutional knowledge to strategic decision-making. Lead or support college level committees related to curriculum, academic policy, and faculty affairs. Scholarly Engagement Maintain an active scholarly agenda and teaching presence that models academic excellence, keeps the Associate Dean connected to the faculty experience, and contributes to the intellectual vitality of the College. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required and assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS and EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers, electronic mail, word processing, database management, spreadsheet software, research statistical and data analysis software as needed. Required Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Doctoral degree in a health-related field. 2. Strong record of academic leadership. 3. Demonstrated achievement of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with appointment at the rank of Professor eligible for tenure. 4. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 5. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 6. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 7. Demonstrated experience working collaboratively. 8. Demonstrated commitment to student and faculty success. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Experience with curriculum development and program promotion. 2. Experience with promotion and tenure processes. 3. Experience with faculty union processes. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/23/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Diversity Statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16869 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Diversity Statement - (justice, equity, diversity and inclusion) Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Doctoral degree in a health-related field? Yes No * Do you have strong record of academic leadership? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated achievement of teaching, scholarship, and service commensurate with appointment at the rank of Professor eligible for tenure? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience working collaboratively? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated commitment to student and faculty success? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
