    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17059": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Campus Recreation/Facilities &amp; Operations",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Campus Recreation/Facilities &amp; Operations Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Coordinator, Campus Recreation/Facilities & Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document: Current or ability to obtain and maintain a valid certificate from the American Red Cross; CPR for adults, infants, and children, AED (Automatic External Defibrillations) and First Aid within the first 30 days of employment (as one complete document). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02209 Job Title Coordinator, Campus Recreation/Facilities & Operations Position Number 109439 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 10 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $60,000 - $68,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Facility Operations Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by October 2, 2026. Applications received after October 2, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The position is an in-person work schedule. POSITION SUMMARY : Under the direct supervision of the Assistant Director, Facilities and Operations, provide leadership and day-to-day oversight and management of staff who serve as the front-line point of contact for all members and visitors. Contribute to the management and care of the Mackal/Keaney/Tootell Complex, Anna Fascitelli Fitness and Wellness Center. Assist with the identification and implementation of the Department’s strategic goals that foster engagement and promote a life-long commitment to holistic well-being for the University of Rhode Island community. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Recruit, select, train, supervise, mentor, schedule, administer payroll, and evaluate a diverse facility operations student staff that includes Recreation Attendants in Mackal Field House and Anna Fascitelli Fitness and Wellness Center, Facilities & Operations student staff, and temporary workers. Work in conjunction with other full-time staff with staff training and other employees’ events (i.e., staff appreciation) with an emphasis on leadership development, student engagement, and a path to success beyond graduation. Assist with the management of facility rental requests and the successful execution of events in Campus Recreation complexes. Responsible for coordinating student and internal groups, outside rentals, and University events including but not limited to: pre-planning arrangements, contract development, event supervision, custodial/maintenance personnel management, and enforcement of safety and risk management rules and regulations. Build collaborative relationships with Department of Campus Recreation program areas/units; as well as external program departments, such as Facilities Operations, Capital Projects, Athletics, Conferences Services, Property & Support Services, Public Safety, Admissions, and other key university stakeholders. Support a culture that promotes collaboration focusing on customer services, safety, quality control, sustainability, and accessibility. Responsible for the overall facilities operations planning and the day-to-day leadership and direction to ensure that the facilities are clean, safe, and accessible. Identify and recommend maintenance projects and capital improvements to enhance user satisfaction and safety. Assist in oversight of the department’s internal custodial and maintenance programs, including outside vendors and contractors. Manage facility repairs and upkeep during annual maintenance shutdowns, semester breaks, and planned and/or emergency facilities projects. Advise management team on departmental policies and procedures related to facility usage, customer service, and member/guest access. Provide input and assist in the development of all emergency policies and procedures; ensure policies are implemented and enforced; conduct routine facility inspections and audits. Assist full-time staff with facilitating Emergency Action Plan training. Track and monitor accident and incident reports within the facilities. Collaborate with the Coordinator of Fitness, Health, and Well-being to create and maintain a comprehensive tracking/inventory/preventative maintenance system, including equipment installation, routine inspections, daily cleaning, and preventative maintenance, to help ensure maximum upkeep of fitness equipment. Procure operating equipment and supplies for facility repairs and upgrades, equipment lending, supplies, and inventory, to include but not limited to: locker/towel service, equipment checkout, quest passes/day passes, and laundry service lost and found. Ensure all cash handling transactions are followed per established policies and procedures. Develop effective customer service policies which improve service levels. Manage facilities key access, ID facility access, surveillance cameras, PA systems, emergency equipment and AED units, Material Safety Data Sheets ( MSDS ), and radios for the department. Assist with management of software systems necessary to keep facilities operational and stay current with industry standards (Connect2, Supltup, Handshake, EMS , ActiveNet, IMLeagues, Fusion, eCampus, etc.) Promote various principles and practices to maximize the department’s sustainability impact on campus; help ensure facilities/spaces are as environmentally responsible as they are functional. Compile key performance indicators, (assessments, learning outcomes, facility statistics, annual management report, etc.), and make recommendations for change when needed. Participate in departmental strategic goals and long-term planning processes. Be involved with and make meaningful contributions to departmental, divisional, and institutional initiatives, as well as within professional organizations. Actively work with other campus departments in student persistence and retention efforts. Serve on various institutional, divisional, and departmental committees. Contribute to an environment that values high expectations, accountability, and balanced lifestyle choices. Work in a team-centered environment and collaborate effectively with fellow colleagues. Attend departmental, divisional, and University meetings. Promote and sustain a culture of transparency, professionalism, integrity, respect, and work in a teamoriented environment. Work on a team that collaborates effectively with fellow colleagues and achieves targeted goals. Continue to develop expert knowledge in area of specialization and serve as a resource to all team members. Participate in benchmarking studies aimed at identifying best practices, expand programs and services, improve facilities, and/or other initiatives which support and enhance student’s engagement and success. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Provide departmental leadership in the development of new, creative open recreation spaces, programs, and services. Assist the Director and Associate Director of Campus Recreation with special projects and directives for the Division of Student Affairs. Work a flexible schedule including some nights and weekend hours. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, word-processing, database management, and spreadsheet software; Current or ability to obtain and maintain CPR , First Aid and Automatic External Defibrillators ( AED ) certifications within the first 30 days of employment. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS : REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Sports Management, Exercise Science, Higher Education, Physical Education or related field. 2. Minimum of two years of full-time experience in the management of a multi-purpose recreational and/or athletic facility. 3. Demonstrated experience in recreation/athletic facilities scheduling. 4. Demonstrated experience in developing facilities usage/rental contracts and invoicing. 5. Demonstrated experience in risk management mitigation. 6. Demonstrated supervisory experience. 7. Demonstrated training experience. 8. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 9. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 10. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 11. Current or ability to obtain American Red Cross CPR , First Aid, and AED certifications within the first 30 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s Degree in Sports Management, Exercise Science, Higher Education, Physical Education or related field. 2. Minimum of two years of full-time experience in the management of a multi-purpose recreational and/or athletic facility in a college or university setting. 3. Demonstrated experience in developing facilities usage/rental contracts and invoicing. 4. Demonstrated experience in facility emergency response. 5. Demonstrated experience in training student employees in a college or university setting with an enrollment over 10,000 students. 6. Demonstrated experience supervising custodial and/or maintenance professionals. 7. Demonstrated experience with recreation environment technology (i.e., SubItUp, ActiveNet, Fusion, EMS , Handshake, Connect2, e-Campus). 8. Current American Red Cross Instructor Certification. 9. Demonstrated evidence of professional involvement in organizations (i.e. NIRSA : Leaders in Collegiate Recreation ( NIRSA ) or other recreation based associations). Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. May be required to work evenings and weekends. Posting Date 09/11/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document: Current or ability to obtain and maintain a valid certificate from the American Red Cross; CPR for adults, infants, and children, AED (Automatic External Defibrillations) and First Aid within the first 30 days of employment (as one complete document). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17049 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Sports Management, Exercise Science, Higher Education, Physical Education or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of full-time experience in the management of a multi-purpose recreational and/or athletic facility? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in recreation/athletic facilities scheduling? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in developing facilities usage/rental contracts and invoicing? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in risk management mitigation? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated training experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have current or ability to obtain American Red Cross CPR, First Aid, and AED certifications within the first 30 days of employment? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
