      "title": "Professor, Nursing",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Professor, Nursing Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Professor, Nursing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Professor, Nursing Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The College of Nursing is searching for a tenure-track Professor to begin Fall 2026. POSITION SUMMARY : The URI College of Nursing is committed to scientific inquiry, knowledge development, and excellence in teaching. We are building a robust research portfolio and are known for our innovative undergraduate and graduate programs that support our mission to prepare nurses to excel as outstanding clinicians, scholars, and leaders who will enhance the health and health care of individuals, families, communities, and populations both locally and globally. We seek a dynamic faculty member to join us as we continue to grow. The successful candidate will have an appointment with the College of Nursing with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the campus and external partners. The candidate will serve as a senior member of the faculty and will be expected to have a program of research supported by extramural funding in an area that complements the mission of the College of Nursing. The successful candidate will also contribute to the University’s teaching mission and participate in service activities. KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Contribute to the undergraduate and graduate teaching mission of the University by mentoring students and teaching courses for the college. Maintain a robust program of research germane to nursing and health that is extramurally funded. Maintain a high level of dissemination of scholarship as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications and presentations at national and international meetings. Provide leadership in innovative and emerging teaching pedagogies, national and/or international professional organizations, and in service to the college through faculty mentorship. Serve on college and University committees. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. PhD degree. 2. Recognized leader in the field at a national/international level (e.g., Fellow in the AAN or AANP ). 3. Eligible for tenure in the College of Nursing. 4. Experience teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels. 5. Research record evidenced by significant external funding (e.g. NIH , AHRQ ). 6. Evidence of publications in established journals. 7. Proficiency in written communication skills. 8. Proficiency in oral communication skills. 9. Strong interpersonal skills. 10. Clinical expertise in area of specialization. 11. Expertise in palliative/end-of-life, community/public health, pediatrics, psychiatric-mental health, gerontology, environmental health, or other area complementary to the faculty and college needs. 12. Ability to write competitive applications for extramural funding. 13. Eligible for RN or APRN licensure in Rhode Island. 14. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations. PREFERRED : Evidence of successful research collaborations. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Dean Nursing Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 109822 Posting Number F00495 Posting Date 11/07/2025 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/15904 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD degree? Yes No * Are you a recognized leader in the field at a national/international level (e.g., Fellow in the AAN or AANP)? Yes No * Are you eligible for tenure in the College of Nursing? Yes No * Do you have experience teaching at undergraduate and graduate levels? Yes No * Do you have a research record evidenced by significant external funding (e.g. NIH, AHRQ)? Yes No * Do you have evidence of publications in established journals? Yes No * Do you have clinical expertise in area of specialization? Yes No * Do you have expertise in palliative/end-of-life, community/public health, pediatrics, psychiatric-mental health, gerontology, environmental health, or other area complementary to the faculty and college needs? Yes No * Do you have ability to write competitive applications for extramural funding? Yes No * Are you eligible for RN or APRN licensure in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17152": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 5 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Statement - describing scholarly accomplishments, future research plans, and vision for building an externally funded research program (as one complete document). (#4) Statement of Teaching - describing teaching philosophy. experience, and potential contributions to the BS Environmental Engineering curriculum (as one complete document to upload). (#5) Other Document - copies of two relevant publications (as one complete document to upload). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title ASSISTANT PROFESSOR, ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/15/2026. Applications received after 11/15/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ URI is Rhode Island’s flagship public research university. In 2025, URI achieved Carnegie R1 status, placing it among the nation’s highest research activity universities. URI was also ranked the No. 1 public university in New England by The Wall Street Journal/College Pulse. The Kingston campus is located near Narragansett Bay and the Atlantic coast, with access to Providence, Boston, New York, and the coastal communities of southern Rhode Island. Rhode Island is also an EPSCoR-eligible jurisdiction, providing faculty with access to targeted federal funding opportunities that support research capacity, collaboration, and innovation. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the assistant professor level in environmental engineering. The anticipated start date is August 2027. We seek an outstanding scholar and educator with the potential to build a nationally prominent, externally funded research program. This is a broad search, and candidates from all areas of environmental engineering are encouraged to apply. The department is interested in reviewing applications from candidates whose work touches on air pollution, indoor air quality, links between climate and air quality, atmospheric chemistry, and ocean–atmosphere interactions; however, candidates from all areas of environmental engineering are encouraged to apply and will receive full consideration. The successful candidate will contribute to the growth of environmental engineering research at URI and help advance the launch and long-term success of URI’s new Bachelor of Science degree program in Environmental Engineering. THE POSITION IS IN- PERSON POSITION SUMMARY : The successful candidate will be expected to develop a nationally recognized and externally funded research program; publish high-impact scholarship; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; mentor undergraduate and graduate students; contribute to the new BS Environmental Engineering curriculum; and participate in service to the department, college, university, profession, and broader community. Applicants are expected to hold a terminal degree in environmental engineering, civil engineering, chemical engineering, environmental health engineering, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Required qualifications include evidence of potential for excellence in research and teaching; a strong record of scholarly activity appropriate to career stage; effective written and oral communication skills; and the ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Preferred qualifications include evidence of potential for external research funding; experience advising or mentoring students; ability to teach core undergraduate or graduate environmental engineering courses; interest in program development; and Professional Engineering licensure or the ability to pursue licensure. The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering is housed within URI’s College of Engineering and is entering an exciting period of growth. The department offers undergraduate and graduate programs in civil and environmental engineering and is launching a new BS degree in Environmental Engineering. The successful candidate will join URI at a pivotal moment, with opportunities to help shape a new undergraduate degree program while expanding the department’s research impact in environmental engineering. Faculty and students in the College of Engineering work in the Fascitelli Center for Advanced Engineering ( FCAE ), a 190,000-square-foot facility designed to support interdisciplinary engineering research and education. Research in the facility is organized around themes that include clean water, sensors and instrumentation, alternative energy, advanced materials, robotics, biomedical technology, and nanotechnology. FCAE also houses the Shimadzu Analytical Core, the RI Water Resources Center, and the RI Consortium for Nanoscience and Nanotechnology. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : • Develop a nationally recognized, externally funded research program in environmentalengineering. • Publish high-impact scholarship. • Teach undergraduate and graduate courses. • Mentor undergraduate, M.S., and Ph.D. students. • Contribute to the development and success of the B.S. in Environmental Engineeringcurriculum. • Participate in service to the department, college, university, profession, and broader community. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, word processing, database management, and spreadsheet software. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. A terminal degree in environmental engineering, civil engineering, chemical engineering, environmental health engineering, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. 2. Evidence of potential for excellence in research and teaching. 3. A strong record of scholarly activity appropriate to the candidate’s career stage. 4. Effective written and oral communication skills. 5. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners. PREFERRED : 1. Evidence of potential to secure external research funding. 2. Experience advising or mentoring students. 3. Ability to teach core undergraduate and/or graduate environmental engineering courses. 4. Interest in Environmental Engineering B.S. degree program development. 5. Professional Engineering licensure or the ability to pursue licensure. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Civil&EnvironmentalEngineering Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 5 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Research Statement – describing scholarly accomplishments, future research plans, and vision for building an externally funded research program (as one complete document). (#4) Statement of Teaching – describing teaching philosophy. experience, and potential contributions to the BS Environmental Engineering curriculum (as one complete document to upload). (#5) Other Document – copies of two relevant publications (as one complete document to upload). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 106442 Posting Number F00529 Posting Date 10/01/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17110 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Statement Statement of Teaching Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will have a terminal degree in environmental engineering, civil engineering, chemical engineering, environmental health engineering, or a closely related field by the time of appointment? Yes No * Do you have evidence of potential for excellence in research and teaching? Yes No * Do you have a strong record of scholarly activity appropriate to the candidate’s career stage? Yes No * Do you have effective written and oral communication skills? Yes No * Do you have ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and external partners? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17078": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02178 Job Title Assistant Director, Student Conduct/ Community Standards Position Number 107615 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level : 11 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $75,000 - $81,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department VP Student Affrs. Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by September14, 2026. Applications received after September 14, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Ensure that student behavior aligns with and supports the University’s mission by investigating and adjudicating community standards violations both on and off campus. Provide proactive education and outreach to the campus community on topics related to community standards. Be responsible for comprehensive case management, data analysis, and the development of educational initiatives aimed at promoting a respectful and safe community environment. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Investigate, adjudicate and maintain accurate records regarding alleged violations of community standards by students and student organizations that include but are not limited to allegations of sexual misconduct, hazing and bullying. Assist in the facilitation and administration of the student conduct process and serve as a resource on community standard matters for students, faculty and staff. Assist with the development of community standards, revisions of policies and procedures, and handbook revisions. Ensure consistency and fairness for all student discipline. Serve as an administrative hearing officer and prepare cases for hearing panels. As needed, assist with the adjudication of Off-campus community standards violations. Collaborate extensively with conduct administrators, Housing and Residential Life staff, Campus Police, faculty and staff regarding student conduct issues. Collect and analyze data regarding student conduct and the conduct system. Develop presentations, statistical reports and summaries as needed. Assist with the ongoing training to ensure that the department is in compliance with Clery regulations and Stop Campus Hazing Act reporting requirements. Manage the data collection and reporting of Clery crimes for the Annual Safety Report in collaboration with URI PD. Assist with the selection, training, and implementation of hearing boards which include faculty, staff and students. Advise hearing panels. Assist with the selection, training, and implementation of conduct advisors, which include faculty, staff and students. Serve as a member of the student conduct team. Participate in the creation and implementation of educational programs and training to prevent violations of community standards. Assist in the development of student conduct/community standards and publication materials, website updates, and training manuals. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Represent the Dean of Students Office on University, Division and other committees and at University events. Work evenings and weekends as necessary. Perform additional duties as necessary. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers; word processing, database management and spreadsheet software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Master’s degree in college student personnel or higher education, or related field. Minimum three years of professional experience in a college setting. Demonstrated evidence of attention to detail and collaborative work style. Demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to support student education and/or student growth. Demonstrated ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations, and to communicate the interpretation to others. Demonstrated ability to prepare and present detailed studies and reports and to make recommendations concerning the substance of the studies and reports. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Demonstrated ability to utilize Maxient software, including analytics. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : Demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment, mediation, conflict resolution and/or campus judicial systems. Demonstrated knowledge of Title IX, Campus Save Act and Clery Act as they relate to sexual assault investigations on college campuses. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/20/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16846 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree in college student personnel or higher education, or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum three years of professional experience in a college setting? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated evidence of attention to detail and collaborative work style? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with evaluation, assessment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to support student education and/or student growth? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to interpret institutional policies, plans, objectives, rules and regulations, and to communicate the interpretation to others? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to prepare and present detailed studies and reports and to make recommendations concerning the substance of the studies and reports? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to utilize Maxient software, including analytics? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
