    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17162": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Academic Advisor Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Academic Advisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02227 Job Title Academic Advisor Position Number 109570 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 10 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $60,000 - $70,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean Arts & Sciences Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/17/2026. Applications received after 10/17/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE OPPORTUNITY FOR A REMOTE / HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE IS POSSIBLE AFTER SIX MONTHS . POSITION SUMMARY : Provide academic advising for undergraduate students. Assigned to designated academic major(s). Provide individual and group advising sessions and workshops to facilitate the transition to college and progression to graduation in a timely manner. Collaborate with staff, faculty, and administration to assist with students’ progress to degree, curriculum materials, and all advising issues to best meet student needs. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Monitor student academic record progression and enrollment status. Update student records in student information system. Initiate student contact, providing proactive advising outreach. Advise students on course, minor, and major curriculum options and readmission throughout the calendar year. Ensure progress toward timely degree completion and communicate with students regarding progress. Collaborate with other advisors, campus departments, and support offices to promote student success and retention efforts. Participate in academic reviews that may include scholastic standing. Attend and assist with planning and executing programs and events as required. Plan and execute events with the living learning community associated with assigned majors. Present, prepare for, and advise during orientation and transfer sessions. Assist students exploring majors. Utilize the student success software to maintain up to date records and notes on students. Create advising materials for students. Routinely review, interpret, and post credit from external sources and escalate as appropriate. Work with experiential/internship and career advisors to provide up-to-date information related to internship, major, and career choices. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Support students from the Community College of Rhode Island ( CCRI ). When appropriate, teach First-Year seminar as assigned. Participate on university committee(s), training(s), conference(s), etc. representing your academic unit as assigned. Advising may include student support, especially in 4+1 and ABM programs when appropriate. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Computers, printers; database management and spreadsheet software; student record-keeping systems. Required Qualifications REQUIRED : 1. Master’s degree with a minimum of two years of experience in academic advising, time as a graduate student included, OR Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of experience providing academic advising in a higher education setting, OR Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of experience advising/counseling (academics, career, non-traditional pathways, etc.) current and/or aspiring college students. 2. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. 3. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 4. Demonstrated experience with data management systems. 5. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 6. Demonstrated experience in and/or dedication to integrating issues of inclusion, equity and social justice in your work. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s degree in college student personnel in higher education and counseling, or a related field. 2. Demonstrated ability to utilize applications, Brightspace (or similar learning management platform), on-line advising, presentation technology and student records systems (i.e., PeopleSoft.). 3. Demonstrated experience with student success platforms (i.e., Starfish). 4. Demonstrated experience working with college students. 5. Demonstrated skills in assessment. _____________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Work evenings and weekends as necessary. Posting Date 10/05/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17158 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree with a minimum of two years of experience in academic advising, time as a graduate student included, OR Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of experience providing academic advising in a higher education setting, OR Bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of experience advising/counseling (academics, career, non-traditional pathways, etc.) current and/or aspiring college students? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with data management systems? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in and/or dedication to integrating issues of inclusion, equity and social justice in your work? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
