    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16516": {
      "title": "Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 5 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter describing your interest and qualifications for the position. (#2) A complete curriculum vitae including the full contact information for at least three professional references (as one complete document). (#3) A research plan, limited to two pages, describing your current and future research and how it relates to the required qualifications (as one complete document). (#4) A narrative, limited to one page, describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). (#5) Other Document - reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (as one complete pdf document). Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant /Associate Professor in Physical Therapy Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by May 11, 2026. Applications received after May 11, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The Department of Physical Therapy at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor with expertise in research and teaching that aligns with the mission of the Department, College, and University. Negotiated rank is contingent on qualifications and experience. This academic-year appointment begins in August 2026. The Department is part of the College of Health Sciences and is nationally recognized for excellence in teaching, research, service, professional leadership, international opportunities for students, strong clinical partnerships, and an on-site clinic. Each year, the program admits a cohort of 32 students who are taught by a dedicated and experienced faculty. The Physical Therapy Department is located on the Kingston campus in a beautiful rural setting just 15 minutes from ocean and bay beaches. The region offers abundant outdoor recreation opportunities, with the Green and White Mountains only a three-hour drive away. The University of Rhode Island provides a rich array of cultural and intellectual events, including theater, music, athletics, and the Honors Colloquium. Additional cultural and recreational opportunities are easily accessible in Providence (40 minutes), Boston and Cape Cod (90 minutes), and New York City (three hours). KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : The successful candidate will: Demonstrate a strong focus on research productivity and obtaining external funding to support research and graduate students. Develop, lead, and collaborate on research programs leading to peer‑reviewed publications and grant submissions in physical therapy or related fields. Teach graduate-level courses in the Doctor of Physical Therapy ( DPT ) program. Contribute service to the Department, College, University, and/or the profession. Mentor and advise students. Demonstrate experience or potential to engage students in teaching, research, and service. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : Ph.D. (or equivalent) completed by August 2027. Eligibility for physical therapist licensure in Rhode Island. Demonstrated ability to establish an independent research agenda and publish in relevant, peer‑reviewed journals. Demonstrated ability to obtain external funding. Demonstrated teaching ability that complements the existing DPT curriculum. Proficiency in oral communication skills. Proficiency in written communication skills. Current membership in the American Physical Therapy Association ( APTA ). Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. PREFERRED : Demonstrated success in securing external research funding. Demonstrated ability to participate in collaborative research. Interest and/or experience in teaching contemporary professional topics in physical therapy at the graduate level. Experience in mentoring graduate students Evidence of success or strong potential for obtaining external funding to support a productive research program. Relevant clinical experience is desirable. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ This is a 9‑month academic‑year position, beginning five days before the start of the Fall 2026 semester and concluding on Commencement Day the following May. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Physical Therapy Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 5 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter describing your interest and qualifications for the position. (#2) A complete curriculum vitae including the full contact information for at least three professional references (as one complete document). (#3) A research plan, limited to two pages, describing your current and future research and how it relates to the required qualifications (as one complete document). (#4) A narrative, limited to one page, describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). (#5) Other Document – reprints of up to 3 publications that you feel best highlight your suitability for the position (as one complete pdf document). Posting Information Position Number 108567 Posting Number F00518 Posting Date 03/11/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16203 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Research Plan A narrative Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will have a Ph.D. (or equivalent) completed by August 2027? Yes No * Do you have eligibility for physical therapist licensure in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to establish an independent research agenda and publish in relevant, peer reviewed journals? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to obtain external funding? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated teaching ability that complements the existing DPT curriculum? Yes No * Do you have current membership in the American Physical Therapy Association (APTA)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17214": {
      "title": "Career Advisor",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Career Advisor Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Career Advisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document - Diversity Statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02238 Job Title Career Advisor Position Number 106007 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 10 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $56,000 - $60,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean, College of Business Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/02/2026. Applications received after 11/02/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide comprehensive career counseling and advising services to undergraduate, graduate, and recent alumni of the College of Business. Guide students through all aspects of career development, including self-assessment, career exploration, job search preparation, interviewing strategies, networking techniques, and the effective use of AI-powered and other web-based career resources. Develop and deliver career education programs, workshops, and advising services for both individuals and groups engaged in the career planning and assessment process. Support the planning and execution of signature events, initiatives, and programs that advance students’ educational and professional goals. Collaborate closely with faculty, staff, student organizations, and partners across the University, including the Center for Career and Experiential Education, to ensure effective referral processes, coordinated student support services, and the integration of career and experiential learning opportunities within the College of Business and across the institution. Duties and Responsibilities KEY ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Counsel and advise College of Business students and recent alumni on career development and career decision-making through individual consultations and group programs. Assist students in identifying career goals, exploring academic and professional pathways, developing job search strategies, and preparing for employment or further education opportunities. Assist in the development, promotion of, and support of the College of Business Career Pathways Program in collaboration with the experiential education coordinator and other career team staff, including the assistant director of employer relations. Design, develop, promote, and facilitate workshops, events, and educational programs that assist students and recent graduates in making informed decisions related to career planning, employment opportunities, further education, and long-term professional development. Work closely with College of Business advisors, experiential education coordinator, academic areas, and student organizations to facilitate cooperation and collaborative programming. Assist in the coordination and support of employer engagement activities, including networking events, employer information sessions, mock interviews, career fairs, and career day event activities, and other internship recruitment initiatives. Guide students in the development of resumes, cover letters, LinkedIn profiles, professional portfolios, and other career-related materials. Assist students in identifying and utilizing AI-powered career tools and other web-based resources to support career exploration, job searching, and professional development. Assist, coordinate, and collaborate with instructors as required for various classes at the college and other career readiness curriculum. Stay current on labor market trends, employer hiring practices, career development theory, and emerging technologies impacting workforce readiness. Participate in departmental, college, and university committees and initiatives that support student retention, engagement, career readiness, and post-graduation success. Assist in other areas as needs arise, working in a flexible manner to continuously improve services. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Participate in College of Business and University of Rhode Island related initiatives and serve on various University committees as needed. Represent the College of Business and Career Services at regional professional associations, conferences, and professional development workshops. Perform additional duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Utilize personal computers, printers, presentation technology, and standard business software applications, including word processing, databases, and spreadsheet programs, to support career advising, program delivery, assessment, and administrative functions. Deliver presentations using digital projection technology and other instructional tools. Maintain the flexibility to work occasional evening and weekend hours to support student programming, employer events, career fairs, and other College and University initiatives. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Master’s degree in higher education, business, career counseling, or a related field. 2. Minimum of two years of experience in direct career counseling to college students at a college or university; Or bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of direct career counseling experience at the institutional level. 3. Demonstrated experience administering, interpreting, and utilizing career assessment tools and career development frameworks to support students’ career exploration, self-assessment, academic planning and career decision making. 4. Demonstrated strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. 5. Demonstrated experience using career services technology platforms, student engagement systems, and talent recruitment tools (e.g., Handshake, 12Twenty, Symplicity CSM , LinkedIn Learning, CareerShift, or similar platforms) to support career advising, employer engagement, experiential learning, and student career outcomes. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience with culturally diverse student populations, as well as with alumni. 2. Demonstrated experience in developing, marketing, and executing career programs. 3. Demonstrated work experience using social media platforms. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document – Diversity Statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17205 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree in higher education, business, career counseling, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of experience in direct career counseling to college students at a college or university; Or bachelor’s degree with a minimum of five years of direct career counseling experience at the institutional level? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience administering, interpreting, and utilizing career assessment tools and career development frameworks to support students’ career exploration, self-assessment, academic planning and career decision making? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience using career services technology platforms, student engagement systems, and talent recruitment tools (e.g., Handshake, 12Twenty, Symplicity CSM, LinkedIn Learning, CareerShift, or similar platforms) to support career advising, employer engagement, experiential learning, and student career outcomes? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
