    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16901": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Honors Program",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Honors Program Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Coordinator, Honors Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02188 Job Title Coordinator, Honors Program Position Number 108353 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 11 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $65,000 - $75,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Honors Program Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 31, 2026. Applications received after August 31, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION WORK SCHEDULE IS IN- PERSON POSTING SUMMARY : Under the direction of the Honors Director, the Program Coordinator manages the day-to-day operations, programming, and budget administration of the Honors Program and the Office of National Fellowships & Academic Opportunities. The Coordinator plays a central role in supporting a dynamic, student-centered environment while helping to implement new initiatives, streamline operations, coordinate complex programming, and foster collaboration across university units. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : 1.Program Operations and Budget Administration Manage the day-to-day administrative operations of the Honors Program and the Office of National Fellowships & Academic Opportunities. Oversee and manage Honors Program and National Fellowships budgets, including purchasing, financial transactions, hiring processes, contracts, summer recontracting, account reconciliation, and related financial processes. Manage URI Foundation accounts and awards. Coordinate office systems, workflows, and operational processes to support efficient and effective program administration. Supervise student employees and support staff operations. 2. Curriculum and Academic Program Coordination Under the direction of the Honors Director, coordinate administrative and logistical support for the University Honors curriculum. Support implementation and ongoing coordination of the evolving interdisciplinary Honors curriculum. Coordinate course scheduling, curriculum processes, and part-time faculty contracts. Collaborate with academic colleges, departments, faculty, and the Faculty Senate Office to support curriculum implementation and academic programming. Provide administrative, operational, and basic technological support to faculty teaching within the Honors Program. Coordinate student advising support related to the interdisciplinary undergraduate Honors curriculum. 3. Honors Colloquium and Public Programming Coordinate and manage logistics for the Honors Colloquium lecture series, including communications, scheduling, speaker contracts, travel and lodging arrangements, budgeting, and event operations. Collaborate with university offices, including Legal Counsel, Publications and Creative Services, Marketing and Communications, Dining Services, Information Technology Services, Campus Police, Facilities, and the Fire Marshal, to support both in-person and virtual events. Support the planning and execution of academically oriented public programming that enhances the visibility and reputation of the Honors Program and the University. Coordinate major Honors events, including seminars, workshops, lectures, expositions, award ceremonies, panel discussions, poster sessions, and the annual undergraduate research conference. Assist in the continued development and execution of new university-wide Honors initiatives and student engagement opportunities. 4. Communications, Outreach, and Engagement Communicate the mission, opportunities, and impact of the Honors Program to prospective students, families, alumni, faculty, donors, and the broader community. Represent the Honors Program at university outreach and recruitment events, including Open House, Welcome Days, Orientation, and related programs. Develop, edit, and manage communications materials in print and digital formats for diverse audiences. Assist in managing Honors Program publications, annual reports, newsletters, website content, and social media platforms. Coordinate publicity and outreach strategies to support Honors events, initiatives, and student success stories. Support website development, maintenance, and digital communications efforts. 5. Student Experience and Residential Collaboration Coordinate with Housing and Residential Life regarding Honors housing initiatives and student programming. Assist in planning and implementing activities that strengthen the Honors student community and enhance student engagement. Support the development of a welcoming, inclusive, and student-centered environment that promotes intellectual curiosity, leadership, and belonging. 6. Data Management and Assessment Collect, organize, and manage programmatic and event-related data, including Honors Program and Honors Colloquium assessment data. Assist with reporting, assessment, and operational tracking to support program evaluation and strategic planning. Coordinate and participate in Honors Program staff meetings and collaborative planning efforts. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform additional duties related to the Honors Program and the Office of National Fellowships & Academic Opportunities as assigned by the Director. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers; Web software, database software, desktop publishing software; all equipment necessary to produce reports, presentations, and publications. Required Qualifications REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree. 2.. Minimum of three years of demonstrated experience in program coordination, event planning, or administrative operations. 3.Demonstrated experience managing budgets and financial processes. 4. Demonstrated strong organizational, project management, and multitasking abilities in a fast-paced environment. 5. Demonstrated ability to develop, implement, and maintain effective operational systems and processes. 6. Demonstrated strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with diverse constituencies, including students, faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners. 8. Demonstrated experience utilizing technology and digital tools to support communications, programming, and operations. 9.Demonstrated ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a highly engaged team environment. 10. Demonstrated commitment to supporting diverse student populations and fostering an inclusive educational environment. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience working in a college or university Honors Program or comparable academic environment. 2. Demonstrated experience supporting curriculum coordination or academic program administration. 3. Demonstrated experience coordinating large-scale public programs or lecture series. 4. Demonstrated supervisory experience. 5. Demonstrated experience with strategic budgeting and financial planning. 6. Demonstrated familiarity with university administrative systems and platforms such as Kuali, Adobe Creative Suite, Excel, Brightspace, Starfish, PeopleSoft, or related systems. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 07/30/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16897 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of demonstrated experience in program coordination, event planning, or administrative operations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience managing budgets and financial processes? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong organizational, project management, and multitasking abilities in a fast-paced environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to develop, implement, and maintain effective operational systems and processes? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to collaborate effectively with diverse constituencies, including students, faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience utilizing technology and digital tools to support communications, programming, and operations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a highly engaged team environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated commitment to supporting diverse student populations and fostering an inclusive educational environment? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
