      "title": "Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover Letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document - Transcripts (unofficial will be accepted too) Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02097 Job Title Research Assistant I (Infectious Diseases Research Laboratory) Position Number 107661 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PTAA - Professional/Tech/Admin Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 1 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $35,000 - $45,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Pharmacy Practice and Clinical Research Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: ( https://jobs.uri.edu ) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes This is a full time, calendar year position currently funded through 06/26/2027 with anticipated renewal contingent upon continued funding, _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by March 28, 2026. Applications received after March 28, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. _________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Under the supervision of the Principal Investigator(s) or designated laboratory supervisor, the employee shall perform delegated duties in support of infectious diseases research conducted within a Biosafety Level ( BSL -2) laboratory. The employee is required to adhere strictly to all institutional, regulatory, and laboratory policies governing safety, compliance, and research integrity. CONDITION OF EMPLOYMENT : Performance of the essential functions listed above, adherence to all safety and compliance requirements, and maintenance of professional conduct are mandatory conditions of this position. The institution reserves the right to modify duties, restrict laboratory access, or terminate employment in cases of non-compliance, unsafe conduct, or failure to fulfill required responsibilities. KEY JOB RESPONSIBILITIES / FUNCTIONS : The following responsibilities are considered essential functions of this position and are mandatory requirements of employment: Research Support and Technical Duties: Perform laboratory research procedures and experimental protocols as assigned. Assist in the preparation, processing, handling, and analysis of biological specimens and research materials. Accurately record experimental data, observations, and procedures in accordance with laboratory standards and institutional policies. Support ongoing research projects through execution of established methods and protocols. Laboratory Equipment and Instrumentation: Properly operate, maintain, calibrate, and store laboratory instruments and equipment. Immediately report equipment malfunctions, safety concerns, or procedural deviations to the laboratory supervisor. Follow all training requirements prior to operating laboratory equipment. Compliance with Biosafety and Regulatory Requirements: Strictly comply with all biosafety, biosecurity, and institutional safety policies, including BSL -2 containment procedures. Maintain compliance with all applicable federal, state, institutional, and laboratory regulations, including but not limited to OSHA , CDC / NIH biosafety guidelines, and institutional Environmental Health and Safety ( EHS ) policies. Properly use personal protective equipment ( PPE ) and follow required safety protocols at all times. Laboratory Conduct and Professional Responsibilities: Work independently and responsibly under supervisory direction. Maintain laboratory cleanliness, organization, and operational readiness. Protect the integrity, confidentiality, and security of research materials, data, and laboratory resources. Complete all required safety, compliance, and laboratory training prior to performing assigned duties and maintain active certification status as required. Work Schedule and Availability Requirements: The employee is required to maintain a flexible schedule based on experimental needs. This position requires availability outside of standard business hours, including early mornings, evenings, and weekends, for the purpose of time-sensitive sample collection, monitoring experiments, or maintaining research continuity. Physical and Environmental Requirements: The employee must be able to perform the essential functions of this position safely and effectively. These requirements include, but are not limited to: Ability to work safely in a BSL -2 laboratory environment with infectious agents. Ability to stand for extended periods of time. Ability to use hands for fine motor tasks, including pipetting, handling specimens, and operating laboratory equipment. Ability to lift and move laboratory supplies and equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. Ability to wear required personal protective equipment, including gloves, lab coat, eye protection, and respiratory protection if required. Ability to perform repetitive laboratory tasks requiring manual dexterity. Duties and Responsibilities OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties, as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers; word processing, database management, spreadsheet software, laboratory equipment. U.S. Citizenship. Required Qualifications REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Microbiology, Biology, or related life sciences field. 2. Demonstrated research experience in a higher education setting. 3. Experience with infectious diseases protocols. 4. Demonstrated organizational skills. 5. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. U.S. Citizenship (to access satellite lab space on Providence Veterans Affairs Campus). _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 03/09/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover Letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document – Transcripts (unofficial will be accepted too) Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16021 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree in Microbiology, Biology, or related life sciences field? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated research experience in a higher education setting? Yes No * Do you have experience with infectious diseases protocols? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated organizational skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have U.S. Citizenship (in order to access satellite lab space on Providence Veterans Affairs Campus)? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PTAA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17216": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Finance and Operations",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Finance and Operations Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Director, Finance and Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02236 Job Title Assistant Director, Finance and Operations Position Number 107090 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 15 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $110,000 - $120,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Kingston Library Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/29/2026. Applications received after 10/29/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION WILL BE IN- PERSON POSITION SUMMARY : Serve as the lead financial and administrative officer for the University Libraries and as a strategic thought partner to the University Librarian. Advise the University Librarian and Library leadership team on matters related to personnel, finance, budgeting, and administration, and lead associated strategic planning, initiatives, and policy development. Develop strategies and recommendations related to the University Libraries’ participation in URI’s incentive-based budget ( IBB ) environment and play an integral role in long-range planning and advancement of the Libraries’ strategic objectives. Serve as a member of the Library executive leadership team. Duties and Responsibilities DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : ● Serve as the senior financial and administrative officer responsible for the Libraries’ administrative, financial, and fiscal management programs. ● Serve as the Libraries’ subject matter expert on the University’s incentive-based budget ( IBB ) model, identifying, recommending, and coordinating strategies that advance short- and long-term Library goals. ● Lead the strategic development, implementation, and management of budgets across the Libraries’ diverse funding sources, including state appropriations, student fees, donor and endowed funds, grants, revenue, and other restricted and unrestricted funds. ● Provide financial guidance and strategic analysis for Library programs, services, and initiatives, including pro forma analysis, project costing, financial modeling, compliance, and vendor contract administration. ● Serve as the principal liaison to University Associate Vice Presidents (AVPs), their designees, and central administrative offices on matters related to budget, finance, human resources, and other operational issues, addressing and resolving interdepartmental concerns as appropriate. ● Lead the development, implementation, monitoring, and periodic review of internal administrative policies, procedures, and records governance frameworks. ● Provide ad hoc financial analyses, expenditure monitoring, short- and long-term forecasting, and advanced financial modeling to identify opportunities for growth and efficiency, as well as potential budgetary risks. Present clear recommendations and risk-mitigation strategies to Library leadership. ● Lead the annual Library budget process, coordinating requests from unit heads and strategically allocating resources across the Libraries’ multiple funding sources and priorities. ● Monitor the availability and use of endowed and other donor-restricted funds, working with Library leadership to ensure funds are used strategically, routinely, and in accordance with donor intent and current Library priorities. ● Coordinate and provide oversight of complex human resources and labor relations processes affecting the Libraries. ● Provide high-level oversight of external post-award grant portfolios, including subaward invoice approvals, revenue projections, overhead allocations, and carryover tracking. ● Manage and direct non-academic Library personnel and foster a responsive organizational structure and workplace culture that positions staff to effectively support Library operations and priorities. ● Participate in University committees and working groups, representing the University Libraries on financial, administrative, operational, and strategic matters as requested. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers and printers; word processing, database management, and advanced spreadsheet software; Microsoft Office Suite, including PowerPoint, Excel, and Access; and enterprise resource planning ( ERP ) systems, such as Oracle, PeopleSoft, and Banner. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in finance, management, public administration, business administration, or a related field, with a minimum of five (5) years of demonstrated professional experience in financial management within a complex organization, including the tracking, analysis, and management of revenue and expenditure budgets and actuals; or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field with a minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible professional experience in financial management within a complex organization. 2. Demonstrated advanced proficiency in spreadsheet applications, data analysis, and financial reporting. 3. Demonstrated professional experience using enterprise resource planning ( ERP ) systems, such as Oracle, PeopleSoft, or Banner, including finance, human resources, student, and/or grant modules. 4. Demonstrated ability to serve as a strategic thought partner to senior leaders and stakeholders across portfolios of varying size and complexity. 5. Demonstrated supervisory experience managing professional staff and complex administrative operations. 6. Demonstrated experience developing complex financial models, short- and long-term forecasts, and pro forma analyses. 7. Demonstrated ability to respond effectively to complex, fast-paced ad hoc requests and deliver clear, concise, and timely reports and recommendations. 8. Demonstrated experience managing administrative operations, vendor contracts, memoranda of understanding (MOUs), or similar agreements within a complex organization. 9. Demonstrated knowledge of resource management and personnel alignment practices within an incentive-based budget environment. 10. Demonstrated strong verbal, written, interpersonal, and presentation skills. 11. Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and manage multiple priorities and projects simultaneously. 12. Demonstrated experience working effectively with diverse groups and populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience working within the University of Rhode Island’s administrative and financial environment, including familiarity with relevant University systems, policies, processes, and organizational structures. 2. Professional experience in an academic or research library or demonstrated experience supporting the financial and administrative operations of a comparably complex academic organization. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/15/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17197 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in finance, management, public administration, business administration, or a related field, with a minimum of five (5) years of demonstrated professional experience in financial management within a complex organization, including the tracking, analysis, and management of revenue and expenditure budgets and actuals; or a Bachelor’s degree in a related field with a minimum of seven (7) years of progressively responsible professional experience in financial management within a complex organization? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated advanced proficiency in spreadsheet applications, data analysis, and financial reporting? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated professional experience using enterprise resource planning (ERP) systems, such as Oracle, PeopleSoft, or Banner, including finance, human resources, student, and/or grant modules? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to serve as a strategic thought partner to senior leaders and stakeholders across portfolios of varying size and complexity? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience managing professional staff and complex administrative operations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience developing complex financial models, short- and long-term forecasts, and pro forma analyses? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to respond effectively to complex, fast-paced ad hoc requests and deliver clear, concise, and timely reports and recommendations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience managing administrative operations, vendor contracts, memoranda of understanding (MOUs), or similar agreements within a complex organization? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge of resource management and personnel alignment practices within an incentive-based budget environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal, written, interpersonal, and presentation skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise sound judgment, and manage multiple priorities and projects simultaneously? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience working effectively with diverse groups and populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
