    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17193": {
      "title": "Cook&#39;s Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Cook&#39;s Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Cook's Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year A generous benefits package including a tuition waiver for CCRI, RIC, and URI for the successful candidate, spouse, and dependents (if applicable) based on current education. paid time off, paid state holidays, and a mandatory retirement plan are also available in addition to many other types of benefits. To learn more about the benefits package, please visit: https://www.exploreemployeebenefits.ri.gov/ URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request a reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. For positions covered by a collective bargaining agreement, the search process may be subject to applicable bargaining unit procedures. The successful candidate will be subject to a pre-employment criminal background report paid for by the University. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number CS02319 Job Title Cook's Helper (Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year) Position Number 215 FTE FLSA Pay Rate Salary Range $33,619 - $35,865 (ACADEMIC YEAR SALARY) PLUS (There is an ADDITIONAL $3,200 annually for shift differential). Pay Grade Level Grade 309 Position Type Classified Civil Service Staff Union C94/L528 - Council 94/Local 528 (Serv/Maint) Status Academic Year, Full-time, Limited Restriction or Limitation Reason Leave to Protect Status End Date of Restriction or Limitation Leave to Protect Status: 4/3/2027 Department Information Department Dining Central Operations Contact(s) Sean Nelson Specialist, Talent Acquisition Office of Human Resources 80 Lower College Road Kingston, RI 02881 Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Sean.nelson@uri.edu Physical Demands At the time of appointment must be physically qualified to perform assigned duties as evidenced by a physician’s certificate. Campus Location Kingston Building(s) Hope Commons (all areas) Grant Funded Extension Contingent on Funding Date Extension Contingency Notes Duties and Responsibilities GENERAL STATEMENT OF DUTIES : To work as a helper to a cook or baker by performing simple tasks in the preparation of foods and beverages (hot or cold) in a kitchen of a state institution; or, to perform food services duties in a dining room or cafeteria served by this kitchen; to work in the food preparation areas or to operate the pan and rack washing machine in the central food processing plant; or to perform those duties necessary to maintain cleanliness in the kitchen and related areas; and to do related work as required. SUPERVISION RECEIVED : To work under the close supervision of a superior from whom are received detailed and explicit instructions; work is reviewed for compliance with such instructions. SUPERVISION EXERCISED : As required, may supervise the work of patient or inmate help. ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLES OF WORK PERFORMED : As assigned to work as helper under the close supervision of a cook by performing such duties as: To wash, peel, chop, dice, or grind vegetables, fruits, and other foods for cooking or for salads; to do other simple work in food preparation such as: making toast, coffee, tea, chocolate; preparing cereal, cooking eggs; making sandwiches; stirring soup; boiling potatoes or other vegetables; to assemble diet trays and as instructed arranges food thereon to be served to patients; loads food onto food trucks or places food in receptacles in steam tables; to set up dining tables for service; and as required to serve food to persons in a cafeteria from steam tables; to collect trays, soiled dishes, cutlery, glassware, etc. after meals and to dispose (swill) of scrap or leftover foods; to wash dishes manually or in an automatic dishwashing machine and to wash cutlery and glassware and to put them in their designated places for reuse; to clean and wash food trucks, dishwashing machines; iceboxes, walk-in refrigerators and other kitchen equipment and utensils; to clean and wash down the kitchen cafeteria and related dining areas; and to do related work as required. As assigned to work as a helper under the close supervision of a baker by performing such duties as: To assemble materials and to weigh, measure, and as instructed mix ingredients by hand or in an electric powered mixing machine; to roll dough, and fill pans with dough or batter; to place good to be baked in, and remove them from ovens; to perform such tasks as carrying materials to a baker or to machines, depositing ingredients in containers, greasing pans, lining pans with greased paper or other appropriate lining; to move racks or rack trucks of dough and/or batter, or baked goods to and from ovens; to clean bakery areas and related equipment and utensils; and to do related work as required. As assigned to work in the central food processing plant by performing such duties as: to work as a helper to cooks, bakers and meat cutters in performing such tasks as assembling, portioning, packaging and transporting of materials, to operate a pan and rack washing machines; to wash pots and pans; to clean work areas and refrigerators; and to do related work as required. Required Qualifications KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS AND CAPACITIES : A familiarity with the methods and procedures applied in the cooking or baking of food, and in food service and in cleaning of kitchen or bakery areas; the ability to understand and follow simple verbal or written directions; the ability to exercise care in the handling, washing, drying and storing of cooking or baking equipment, and glassware; and related capacities and abilities. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE : EDUCATION : Sufficient to follow simple verbal directions; and EXPERIENCE : Such as may have been gained through employment as a helper in a kitchen or bakery in a hospital, hotel or restaurant which required the performance of routine work in food preparation, food service and various tasks incidental to the preparation of food in a kitchen or bakery, and food service in a dining room or cafeteria. OR- any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Work Hours Wednesday & Thursday – 11:30 am to 10:00 pm Friday & Saturday – 1:30 pm to 12:00 am Work hours and days off will vary during the month of August, J-Term, and Spring Break period Academic year dates are 08/09/26 through 05/15/27 Posting Date 10/13/2026 Closing Date 10/22/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Full-Time, 40 hrs., Academic Year A generous benefits package including a tuition waiver for CCRI , RIC , and URI for the successful candidate, spouse, and dependents (if applicable) based on current education. paid time off, paid state holidays, and a mandatory retirement plan are also available in addition to many other types of benefits. To learn more about the benefits package, please visit: https://www.exploreemployeebenefits.ri.gov/ URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request a reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. For positions covered by a collective bargaining agreement, the search process may be subject to applicable bargaining unit procedures. The successful candidate will be subject to a pre-employment criminal background report paid for by the University. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17131 Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a State employee who is a member of AFSCME/Council 94? Yes--IF YES, I understand that if I am the most senior lateral transfer bidder, fully qualified and in good standing, that I MUST ACCEPT THIS POSITION. No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17022": {
      "title": "Catering Coordinator",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Catering Coordinator Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Catering Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02192 Job Title Catering Coordinator Position Number 109348 FTE 1.00 FLSA Non-Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 9 Pay Grade Range Anticipated Hiring Salary Range: $55,000 - $60,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dining Catering Operations Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by August 28, 2026. Applications received after August 28, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide administrative, operational, fiscal, and customer service support for URI Dining Catering and Events. Serve as the day-to-day primary coordinator for event administration, client communications, billing, event documentation, scheduling, and logistical support for catering operations. Support the General Manager, Catering and Events, in all unit efforts as needed. Assist with sales activities, event logistics, financial administration, customer service, marketing initiatives, and operational coordination. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Serve as the primary point of contact for routine catering inquiries and event requests. Receive, review, process, and maintain catering orders utilizing designated event management and catering software systems. Assist clients in identifying event needs, menu selections, service requirements, room setups, equipment needs, and logistical details. Prepare event documentation, banquet event orders, invoices, contracts, estimates, and related operational reports. Coordinate communication among clients, culinary staff, operations staff, facilities personnel, vendors, and University departments to ensure successful event execution. Maintain event calendars, staffing schedules, production schedules, delivery schedules, and operational timelines. Assist the General Manager in planning and coordinating conferences, donor events, commencement activities, VIP functions, and special events as needed. Assist with event setup verification, event execution, and post-event follow-up activities. Maintain customer records, sales data, historical event information, and operational files. Process invoices, deposits, billing documents, journal entries, and other financial records while assisting with budget tracking, sales reporting, revenue monitoring, and operational performance reporting. Compile and prepare reports related to sales, customer satisfaction, event activity, labor utilization, and financial performance. Assist with recruiting, onboarding, training, scheduling, and supervising student employees assigned to catering operations. Ensure compliance with University policies, food safety regulations, risk management procedures, and departmental operating standards. Work collaboratively with all University departments to support operational success. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, catering management software, event management software, point-of-sale systems, CBORD /Food Service Suite, EMS , Microsoft Office applications, financial management systems, database software, and related technology is preferred. Must possess and maintain: • Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification • TIPS or equivalent Responsible Alcohol Service Certification • Valid Rhode Island Driver’s License Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Event Management, Communications, Marketing, Food Service Management, or a related field. 2. Minimum of two years of professional experience in catering, hospitality, conference services, event management, customer service, sales support, foodservice operations, or a related field. 3. Demonstrated experience coordinating events, schedules, logistics, or customer service activities. 4. Demonstrated customer service and communication skills. 5. Must have Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification and TIPS Certification or obtain both within six months of appointment. 6. Ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience in higher education dining, conference services, hospitality, or event management. 2. Experience with Microsoft Office applications including Word, Excel, Outlook, and PowerPoint. 3. Experience using CBORD Food Service Suite, EMS , CaterTrax, or similar hospitality management systems. 4. Experience with billing, budgeting, accounts receivable, or financial reporting. 5. Experience supervising student employees. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. This position may require frequent evening and weekend work in support of special events, commencement activities, conferences, and catering operations. Posting Date 08/14/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16947 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in hospitality management, Business Administration, Event Management, Communications, Marketing, Food Service Management, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of professional experience in catering, hospitality, conference services, event management, customer service, sales support, foodservice operations, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience coordinating events, schedules, logistics, or customer service activities? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated customer service and communication skills? Yes No * Do you have Rhode Island Food Safety Manager Certification and TIPS Certification or obtain both within six months of appointment? Yes No * Do you have ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
