    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17202": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Lab Manager Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Lab Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02232 Job Title Lab Manager Position Number PS# 00008221 FTE 0.57 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 10 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $55,000 - $65,000 (Salary will be prorated as position is part-time 20-Hours per week work schedule) Status Calendar Year, Part-time, Limited Department Information Department Cell & Molecular Biology Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes Position is part-time 20-hours per week, calendar year, limited to 07/22/2027 with anticipated renewal. Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/01/2026. Applications received after 11/012026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Remote work could be possible for some tasks (e.g., documentation & data analysis), but it is unlikely for most of the work responsibilities as the position needs to perform work in the Lab. POSITION SUMMARY : The lab manager will oversee day-to-day operations of an environmental microbial ecology laboratory focused on the molecular and microscopic identification of unknown protists, particularly from marine sedimentary environments. The successful candidate will manage daily research activities, lead hands-on training of students, and contribute to the development of laboratory technologies and protocols. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : ● Maintain detailed up-to-date laboratory notebooks, utilize safe laboratory protocols, and keep the laboratory organized and in high-functioning condition. ● Maintain laboratory supplies inventory; anticipate needed supplies; place and expedite orders for supplies; verify receipt of supplies. ● Maintain laboratory equipment performance; develop operations, quality, and troubleshooting procedures; arrange equipment replacement, service, and repair. ● Maintain quality checks on safety of laboratory, including biohazards, gas tanks, and ensure maintenance of the facilities according to Good Laboratory Practices. ● Standardize and implement laboratory protocols for field sampling, microbial culture maintenance, microscopic imaging, and high-throughput sequencing (both short- and long-read platforms). ● Design and administer guidelines for data entry and data management in consultation with the principal investigator. ● Independently perform day-to-day laboratory work in conjunction with other lab personnel; help with new trainee onboarding by offering technical and safety trainings. ● Coordinate and perform field sampling for the establishment of time-series data. ● Contribute to the development of new lab technologies and to achieve project objectives in creative and effective ways. ● Document and report experimental results and methods for timely publication and grant applications. ● Work closely with the Principal Investigator to provide timely updates and report project progress. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Proficiency with standard office software (e.g., Microsoft Office, Google Workspace), laboratory information management systems, and scientific communication tools. Familiarity with bioinformatics tools and command-line environments is a plus. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree or higher in microbiology, microbial ecology, marine science, or a related life science discipline. 2. Minimum of two years of experience as a laboratory technician or research staff. 3. Demonstrated experience in one or more of the following: soil or sedimentary microbiology, microbiome identification, next-generation sequencing, ecology and physiology of marine microeukaryotes. 4. Demonstrated strong interpersonal skills. 5. Demonstrated oral and written communication skills. 6. Demonstrated ability to organize, coordinate, and supervise research projects . 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups and cross disciplines. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience in preparing high-throughput sequencing libraries with marine sedimentary samples and/or low-input DNA . 2. Demonstrated experience in bioinformatics analyses of microbiome data. 3. Demonstrated experience in protist genomics/transcriptomics. 4. Demonstrated experience in advanced microscopy. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The position primarily involves indoor laboratory work. Occasional field sampling in coastal or marine environments may involve exposure to outdoor conditions, including sun, wind, and wet/muddy terrain. Posting Date 10/14/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17174 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree or higher in microbiology, microbial ecology, marine science, or a related life science discipline? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of experience as a laboratory technician or research staff? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in one or more of the following: soil or sedimentary microbiology, microbiome identification, next-generation sequencing, ecology and physiology of marine microeukaryotes? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated oral and written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to organize, coordinate, and supervise research projects? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups and cross disciplines? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17055": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Physics – (2 Positions)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor of Physics – (2 Positions) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Professor of Physics – (2 Positions) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 4 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae - (education, previous appointments, publications, talks, presentations, lectures, conferences, awards, special skills (as one complete document). (#3) Statement of Teaching - statement on teaching approach and emphasis in undergraduate and graduate courses (1 page max - as one complete document). (#4) Research Plan - outline of planned research program backed up by demonstrated expertise (4 pages max - as one complete document). Note: Applicants are responsible for having letters from the 3 references sent by email to: searchphysics@etal.uri.edu Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Physics – (2 Positions) Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by October 15, 2026. Applications received after October 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The University of Rhode Island is the State’s flagship land/sea/space grant research university with an enrollment of approximately 18,000 students. The Physics Department has 22 full-time faculty/staff members and offers BS, MS and PhD degrees. URI is in Kingston, RI — a beautiful seaside community that is well connected by car and rail located about an hour away from Boston and 3 hours from New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The Physics Department at the University of Rhode Island ( URI ) invites applications for two full-time tenure-track positions at an Assistant Professor level beginning in the fall of 2027, specifically for theorists or computational physicists working in the field of Quantum Information Science ( QIS ). The Department has established multiple new QIS -related degree programs and research groups that include over $8.5M in external funding. Considerations will be given to applicants who can show expertise and creative ideas for their role as researcher, mentor, and teacher in the QIS program. Applicants working or interested in quantum algorithms, quantum optics, quantum resource theory, and semi-conductor/superconducting quantum computing are encouraged to apply. Points of contact with ongoing research programs in ultrafast spectroscopy, nonlinear optics, astrophysics/gravitation, biological physics, statistical physics, surface and thin film physics are a plus. The Physics Department, College of Arts and Sciences and URI are committed to building and supporting a diverse, inclusive, and equitable community of students and scholars. POSITION SUMMARY : The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate physics courses, advise undergraduate and graduate students toward BS, MS, and PhD degrees, conduct independent and collaborative research, with an expectation of external funding, and be active in service at the levels of Department, College, and University. The successful candidate will also seek collaborations with other researchers at URI including those in Computer Science, Mathematics, Graduate School of Oceanography, Engineering and the Institute for AI and Computational Research. QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : PhD in Physics or a very closely related field. Postdoctoral experience. Record of scholarly achievement (publications, presentations, awards). Demonstrated ability to be an effective teacher of undergraduate and/or graduate physics courses. Demonstrated potential for developing and sustaining an independent, externally funded, research program involving undergraduate and graduate students leading to peer-reviewed publications. Demonstrated proficiency in written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. PREFERRED : 1. Experience in quantum algorithms and quantum information theory. 2. A broader interest in the interdisciplinary field of quantum information science. 3. Demonstrated interest and commitment to increasing the participation of underrepresented students in science through teaching and mentoring. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union Tenure Track Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Physics Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 4 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae – (education, previous appointments, publications, talks, presentations, lectures, conferences, awards, special skills (as one complete document). (#3) Statement of Teaching – statement on teaching approach and emphasis in undergraduate and graduate courses (1 page max – as one complete document). (#4) Research Plan – outline of planned research program backed up by demonstrated expertise (4 pages max – as one complete document). Note: Applicants are responsible for having letters from the 3 references sent by email to: searchphysics@etal.uri.edu Posting Information Position Number 109065 & 106385 Posting Number F00528 Posting Date 09/10/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17041 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Research Plan Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a PhD in Physics or a very closely related field? Yes No * Do you have Postdoctoral experience? Yes No * Do you have record of scholarly achievement (publications, presentations, awards)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to be an effective teacher of undergraduate and/or graduate physics courses? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated potential for developing and sustaining an independent, externally funded, research program involving undergraduate and graduate students leading to peer-reviewed publications? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written and oral communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
