    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17088": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Student Experience and Community Building",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Dean for Student Experience and Community Building Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Dean for Student Experience and Community Building Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Other Document - diversity statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02213 Job Title Assistant Dean for Student Experience and Community Building Position Number 108669 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 14 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $80,000 - $90,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Dean Health Sciences Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/28/2026. Applications received after 10/28/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The College of Health Sciences includes seven departments (Communicative Disorders, Human Development and Family Science, Kinesiology, Nutrition, Physical Therapy, Psychology, and Public Health), as well as the Interdisciplinary Neuroscience Program, the Osher Lifelong Learning Institute, and the Program in Gerontology. The College offers seven undergraduate degrees with a total enrollment of 2,460 students. The College offers eight master’s degree programs and four doctoral degree programs with a total graduate enrollment of 264 graduate students. There are 90 faculty members in the college. The College operates five on campus clinics and two off campus clinics, as well as two child development centers. POSITION SUMMARY : The Assistant Dean of Student Experience and Community Building will work closely with the college leadership, faculty and students, as well as campus partners to develop and implement strategies to enhance the student experience from recruitment through graduation, including supporting admissions efforts and creating community-building opportunities. The Assistant Dean works closely with the CHS student services leadership and staff on joint projects, events, and strategies that promote student success and support an inclusive, student-centered environment. While the major focus will be on student experience, the Assistant Dean will support the planning and implementation of events, communication strategies and other community building activities that foster a college wide sense of belonging, engagement and community among faculty, staff, students and alumni. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop, implement, and assess initiatives that foster a sense of belonging, engagement, and community among students. Plan and execute college-wide events and programs that enhance the student experience. Build and maintain partnerships with campus offices such as Student Affairs, New Student Transitions, Office of Community, Equity and Diversity, Residential Life, and the Fannon Institute for Student Success, to coordinate initiatives that enhance the overall student experience. Collaborate with student organizations and leaders to support involvement, leadership development, and community-building efforts. Lead and oversee the development of peer mentoring and student ambassador programs for the college. Develop and contribute to co-curricular strategies that support yield and sustained engagement from pre-matriculation through graduation. Identify barriers to student retention and collaborate with campus partners to implement proactive, student-centered solutions. Serve as a resource for faculty regarding student engagement and sense of belonging. Collaborate with CHS Student Services on student success and student support initiatives. Lead or support programming that enhances the student journey and contributes to a positive, inclusive learning environment. Coordinate with faculty and staff to support engagement opportunities such as workshops, events, and co-curricular experiences. Serve on committees, working groups, and initiatives related to student experience, belonging, and success. Work closely with the Office of Community, Equity and Diversity ( CED ) and other university entities to help cultivate an environment that fosters an inclusive people-centered culture at the University of Rhode Island. Serve on University Diversity Council ( UDC ). Share best practices across academic and administrative units. Evaluate collective progress toward Focus URI KPIs. Coordinate community building activities to increase impact and eliminate silos. Help plan and implement communication strategies to enhance student experience and community building. Work with the college leadership to develop strategic direction for student experience and community building initiatives across the College of Health Sciences. Provide strategic leadership for college-wide events and signature programs that enhance visibility, strengthen community, and support recruitment, yield, and retention goals. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : When appropriate, teach First-Year seminar as assigned. Participate in college committees. Represent the College in university-wide meetings and with external partners Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, and relevant programs and software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Master’s degree in education, leadership, counseling, college student personnel or related field. 2. Minimum of five years working in a professional capacity with undergraduate and/or graduate students. 3. Demonstrated experience and dedication to enhancing student belonging. 4. Demonstrated experience in program development and facilitation. 5. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with decision makers and stakeholders at multiple levels. 6. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 7. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 8. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience with identifying and mitigating issues and barriers associated with student success. 2. Demonstrated knowledge of program evaluation and assessment. 3. Demonstrated working knowledge of scholarly research and/or best practices regarding issues related to institutional access and community building. 4. Demonstrated experience with communication strategies such as newsletters, website and social media. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Work evenings and weekends as necessary. Posting Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Other Document – diversity statement. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17069 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master’s degree in education, leadership, counseling, college student personnel or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of five years working in a professional capacity with undergraduate and/or graduate students? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience and dedication to enhancing student belonging? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in program development and facilitation? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with decision makers and stakeholders at multiple levels? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16521": {
      "title": "Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) CV with contact information for three (3) professional references (outside URI), as one complete document. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Part-time Faculty, User Experience Graduate Certificate Program Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ Qualified candidates who are not selected for employment for fall semester 2024 will have their applications remain active for two (2) years should a future opportunity arise during the 2025–2026 instructional year, September 1, 2025–August 31, 2026. The Department of Professional and Public Writing in the Harrington School of Communication and Media and College of Arts and Sciences seeks part-time faculty to teach online graduate courses for the UX Graduate Certificate Program on a per-course basis. Areas of instruction include ethical foundations of UX design, UX research and methods, UX and microcopy writing, and interaction design. As the largest college at the University of Rhode Island, the College of Arts and Sciences brings together and supports undergraduate programs across the arts, humanities, sciences, and social sciences. The college is committed to excellence in teaching and its academic units create learning experiences that stress the free and rigorous pursuit of knowledge, intellectual curiosity, respect for differences across cultures and perspectives, a passion for personal expression, and an investment in the responsibilities of an educated global citizen in a democratic society. The College facilitates students’ development into leaders and global citizens who think critically and creatively, communicate effectively, and participate actively in local and global communities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : A selected candidate will teach one (1) or two (2) courses in the Department of Professional and Public Writing. Courses are asynchronous and delivered in an accelerated 7-week format. Part-time faculty are not required to engage in research or service activities but must hold regular office hours and be available to assist students enrolled in their courses. They are expected to stay current in their fields of instruction and with pedagogical methods and instructional technologies. Online teaching requires certification and possibly training by the University. Courses are three (3) credits. Specific responsibilities include: Delivering online lessons and assignments in UX Design principles, tools, and techniques through our course management platform (Brightspace) Providing regular feedback, guidance, and mentoring support to students to facilitate their learning and skill development while conveying confidence in every student’s ability to learn Cultivating a collaborative and participatory online learning environment that values diversity of people, ideas, cultures, and forms of expression Evaluating student performance and progress and providing timely assessment Fostering a safe environment that respects the diversity of people and ideas by modeling respect for all students and conveying confidence in every student’s ability to learn Qualifications: Required: 1. Master’s degree in technical communication or related field or a bachelor’s degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UX research, UX analytics, UX writing and/or content design, usability and heuristic evaluation, accessibility, wireframing/prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy. 2. Must have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools. Preferred: 1. Teaching experience at the college level. 2. For candidates with master’s degrees, professional experience in the field of UX. ______________________________________________________________________________________________________ The University of Rhode Island is an equal-opportunity employer. It is the policy of the University of Rhode Island to provide reasonable accommodation when requested by a qualified applicant or employee with a disability. Union Non-Union Faculty Status Academic Year, Part-time End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Professional & Public Writing Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) CV with contact information for three (3) professional references (outside URI ), as one complete document. Posting Information Position Number N/A - Internal Payroll Posting Number F00417 Posting Date 05/22/2024 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/13400 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Master's degree in technical communication or related field or a bachelor's degree and three (3) years of professional experience in areas such as UX research, UX analytics, UX writing and/or content design, usability and heuristic evaluation, accessibility, wireframing/prototyping, and/or content optimization and strategy? Yes No * Do you have technical knowledge and proficiency in interaction design technologies (e.g., Figma) and the Adobe Suite, as well as remote collaboration tools? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17215": {
      "title": "Manager, Turfgrass and Athletic Grounds",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Manager, Turfgrass and Athletic Grounds Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Manager, Turfgrass and Athletic Grounds Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 4 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) A valid drivers license. (#4) Other Document - Pesticide certification (commercial applicator). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02239 Job Title Manager, Turfgrass and Athletic Grounds Position Number 108520 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 12 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $90,000 - $100,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Facilities Operations Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Manage the daily operations of Athletics Lands and Ground workers. Oversee the University’s turf areas and other sports field surfaces, including campus landscapes and athletic/recreation fields. Design and execute maintenance plans to provide aesthetic and functional turf using best management practices. Communicate and coordinate varsity sports fields and recreation fields use with the Department of Athletics, Department of Recreation, and Special Events Staff. Develop maintenance operating standards and specifications for commercial equipment, landscape maintenance, turf maintenance, construction, and winter operations. Manage and verify hourly time entry and related records for department personnel. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and implement best management practices to achieve the highest possible standard for the University’s recreational and intercollegiate sports fields, including natural grass and synthetic turf surfaces in addition to other exterior sport facility surfaces. Collaborate with and make recommendations to University Facilities Operations and Athletics Departments to develop a systematic approach to turfgrass management with a goal of developing exceptional quality playing surfaces for the University’s student athletes, visitors, and external users. Supervise operations and assigned workers in the division of Athletics Grounds. Act as secondary supervisor for the Campus Grounds division operations and assigned workers. Manage, inspect, and document construction, renovation, and deferred maintenance projects. Manage construction and maintenance contracts for Facilities Operations and provide oversight for landscape projects for other University departments, including Campus Planning and Design and the office of Capital Program Design and Delivery. Manage the summer use of athletic and recreational sports fields and coordinate with external customers to optimize revenue opportunities and showcase campus facilities. Write specifications to procure equipment and materials. Develop written project specifications. Coordinate with the Procurement department for ordering of equipment, materials, and other required services. Directly supervise one small engine mechanic and oversee maintenance of all Turf and Landscape Equipment within Athletics Lands and Grounds. Assist with Campus Grounds Turf and Landscape Equipment maintenance when needed. Develop preventive maintenance schedules for vehicles and equipment. Coordinate with the Automotive department for repairs and maintenance to department fleet vehicles. Exercise knowledge of function and ability to operate and perform adjustments and maintenance on: reel mower cutting units, commercial sprayers, tractors, aerifiers, topdressers, fertilizer and seed application equipment, field painting equipment including robotic autonomous marking equipment, and paint removal equipment. Operate, maintain, and repair irrigation systems for sports fields and landscape areas. Provide oversight and recordkeeping for the application of turf chemicals and pesticides. Provide oversight for accurate field layout and installation, painting sports fields lines, logos, and other markings. Provide management oversight for grounds crews working Athletic department sports events. Manage snow removal operations to include state employees, students, and contractors. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Coordinate and collaborate with university turfgrass experts on research and outreach activities. Coordinate with Athletics’ Operations and Coaching staffs to provide timely setup needs for field facilities and events. Develop and implement projects on the University’s sports turf areas, to include field resurfacing, drainage improvements, irrigation improvements and other construction as needed. Establish and cultivate collaborative relationships with university faculty/staff, strategic partners, turf industry representatives, and professional turf organizations in Rhode Island and the Northeast Region. Evaluate and provide recommendations on products, tools, and equipment used to cultivate, maintain, and use University turf areas. Train employees on equipment operation, pesticide application, and other department procedures and safety protocols. Manage and disseminate Personal Protective Equipment to Lands & Grounds employees. Work in partnership with the Manager, Lands and Grounds to oversee daily Lands & Grounds operations. Coordinate and work closely with the URI Coordinator, Recycling and Solid Waste Management for campus litter cleanup tasks and trash/recycling removal. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers; word processing, database management, and spreadsheet software; cell phone; pesticide certification (commercial applicator); RI hoisting license within 6 months of hire; valid driver’s license; willingness to travel throughout the State and region. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in Plant Sciences, Turfgrass Management, Turf Pathology, or related field. 2. Minimum of five years of hands-on combined experience in turfgrass management, commercial agriculture, and/or closely related field. 3. Demonstrated supervisory experience (including overseeing athletic and recreational NCAA level of playing fields). 4. Demonstrated knowledge of turfgrass equipment maintenance and repair. 5. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. Valid driver’s license. 9. RI hoisting license within six months of appointment. 10. Pesticide certification (commercial applicator). 11. Willingness to travel throughout the State and region. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s degree in turfgrass, plant, environmental science, or business administration. 2. Minimum of five years hands-on experience working in university facilities management or professional sports field management (including managing union workers). 3. Commercial Pesticide License Category 3B. 4. CDL class B driver license. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is frequently exposed to ambient environmental conditions, to include extreme weather conditions. Must be willing to work outside and with pesticides. Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date 11/01/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 4 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) A valid drivers license. (#4) Other Document – Pesticide certification (commercial applicator). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17212 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Required License Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in Plant Sciences, Turfgrass Management, Turf Pathology, or related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of five years of hands-on combined experience in turfgrass management, commercial agriculture, and/or closely related field? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience (including overseeing athletic and recreational NCAA level of playing fields)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated knowledge of turfgrass equipment maintenance and repair? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have a valid driver’s license? Yes No * Will you have RI hoisting license within six months of appointment? Yes No * Do you have pesticide certification (commercial applicator)? Yes No * Do you have willingness to travel throughout the State and region? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
