    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17173": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellow (Vaccine Research)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Postdoctoral Fellow (Vaccine Research) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Postdoctoral Fellow (Vaccine Research) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02229 Job Title Postdoctoral Fellow (Vaccine Research) Position Number 109388 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 99 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $63,240 - $77,076 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Biomedical & Pharmaceutical Sc Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes Position is full-time calendar year, limited to 08/31/2030 with anticipated renewal. ______________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 12/04/2026. Applications received after 12/04/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION IS IN- PERSON POSITION SUMMARY : The Biomedical & Pharmaceutical Sciences Department at the University of Rhode Island ( URI ) invites application of a postdoctoral position to conduct vaccine-related research. The successful postdoctoral fellow is expected to design and develop next-generation of vaccines based on our proprietary platforms and conduct in vivo animal studies to evaluate vaccine efficacy and safety. Post-doctoral fellowship is initially for one year, but it may be renewed annually based on progress. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : ● Design and develop next-generation vaccines and evaluate vaccine efficacy and safety in preclinical animal models. ● Collect, analyze, interpret, and present experimental data using appropriate statistical methods. ● Prepare manuscripts for publication in peer-reviewed journals. ● Contribute to the preparation and writing of grant proposals. ● Present research findings at laboratory meetings and scientific conferences. ● Mentor and train graduate and undergraduate students in laboratory techniques, experimental design, and data analysis. ● Collaborate with other investigators to advance research projects. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, word processing, database management and spreadsheet software. Research computing and advanced data analysis. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Immunology, Virology, Biomedical Sciences, or a closely related field. 2. Extensive hands-on experience in molecular cloning, immunological assays, and animal models. 3. Demonstrated ability to design and execute independent research projects. 4. Strong data analysis, scientific writing, and communication skills. 5. A publication record commensurate with the career stage. 6. Ability to work collaboratively. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Experience in vaccine development and preclinical evaluation. 2. Experience in manuscript and grant writing. 3. Previous experience mentoring students. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/07/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17165 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Ph.D. in Molecular Biology, Immunology, Virology, Biomedical Sciences, or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have extensive hands-on experience in molecular cloning, immunological assays, and animal models? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to design and execute independent research projects? Yes No * Do you have strong data analysis, scientific writing, and communication skills? Yes No * Do you have a publication record commensurate with the career stage? Yes No * Do you have ability to work collaboratively? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
