    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17093": {
      "title": "Staff Physician, Clinical Practice",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Staff Physician, Clinical Practice Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Staff Physician, Clinical Practice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02206 Job Title Staff Physician, Clinical Practice Position Number 109013 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union URI Physicians' Assoc Pay Grade Level N/A Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: (position is hourly with an estimated annual (academic year) salary of $175,000 - $200,000 Status Full-time, Permanent, Academic Year Department Information Department Health Svs. Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/12/2026. Applications received after 10/12/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ (Please note: Work is scheduled and performed during academic year (late August – mid May) and salary is paid on calendar year basis.) ________________________________________________________________________________________________ The position is an in-person work schedule. POSITION SUMMARY : Participate as a member of the health care delivery team that provides primary care services to patients, diagnoses and manages acute and chronic health problems, and contributes to health promotion and disease prevention efforts in partnership with the patient. Serve as a health care and wellness resource for the campus community, and, working in a collaborative environment, focus on educating the patient as well as on providing quality care. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Collaborate with health care delivery team to provide culturally competent primary ambulatory health care services to and in partnership with eligible patients through diagnosis and management of acute and chronic medical conditions. Obtain health histories, perform physical examinations, conduct objective and subjective patient assessment, order diagnostic tests/studies, establish care plan, order medication, and educate the patient appropriate to her/his age, culture, and individual needs. Assure adequate follow-up by obtaining consultations and/or referrals when appropriate. Perform diagnostic and therapeutic procedures including, but not limited to, suturing, wound care, splinting, soft tissue injury, women’s health. Provide proficiency in primary care ambulatory medicine to include interpretation of basic testing (ECGs, PFTs, x-ray wet reads, etc.). Provide advice to athletes participating in intercollegiate, club, and intramural sports, and individual recreation. Advise the Medical Director, Director, and staff on clinical issues and policies, changes in primary care, specialty referrals, resource requirements, and relationships with the campus and local communities. Provide counseling and education to improve health outcomes through application of holistic approach to patient needs. Provide expertise in the recognition and management of routine mental health conditions. Provide comfort and willingness to communicate and share patients with the campus counseling center. Participate in the development and implementation of patient care guidelines focused on quality outcomes. Collaborate with other health care providers (e.g., MD, DO, NP, PA, PCNS ) and professionals (e.g., pharmacists, RN, LPN , CLS , RT, MA, etc.) in the delivery of quality care. Maintain clinical records in accordance with current policies and procedures. Represent the Student Health Service and its programs across campus and within the community. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Rhode Island Medical License (hold or obtain prior to start date); DEA License; Board Certification in a Primary Care Specialty that includes the care of young adults; personal computer, printer; word processing, electronic health record. Required Qualifications REQUIRED : 1. Must hold or obtain an unrestricted Rhode Island Medical License prior to appointment. 2. Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathy (DO) Degree from an accredited medical school. 3. Valid DEA License; 4. Board Certification or eligibility in an appropriate specialty (Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Pediatrics, and/or Emergency Medicine) that includes the care of young adults. 5. Minimum two years of demonstrated post-residency experience in ambulatory primary care. 6. Demonstrated clinical competence in the delivery of healthcare to late adolescents and young adults. 7. Demonstrated qualification for credentialing and medical staff association at supporting hospital. 8. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal skills. 9. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with patients, staff, and community. 10. Demonstrated experience with electronic health records/practice management software. 11. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/population. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated experience, beyond residency, in outpatient primary care medicine. 2. Demonstrated experience, beyond residency, in adolescent medicine (including: office gynecology, orthopedics, and dermatology). 3. Demonstrated experience and/or additional training in psychiatry/behavioral medicine). 4. Demonstrated experience and/or additional training in sports medicine. 5. Demonstrated experience in college health. 6. Demonstrated experience in treatment of eating disordered patients. 7. Demonstrated experience with participation in accreditation. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 09/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17051 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you hold or obtain an unrestricted Rhode Island Medical License prior to appointment? Yes No * Do you have a Doctor of Medicine (MD) or Doctor of Osteopathy (DO) Degree from an accredited medical school? Yes No * Do you have a Valid DEA License? Yes No * Do you have Board Certification or eligibility in an appropriate specialty (Family Medicine, Internal Medicine, Pediatrics, and/or Emergency Medicine) that includes the care of young adults? Yes No * Do you have a minimum two years of demonstrated post-residency experience in ambulatory primary care? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated clinical competence in the delivery of healthcare to late adolescents and young adults? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated qualification for credentialing and medical staff association at supporting hospital? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with patients, staff, and community? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with electronic health records/practice management software? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/population? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
