    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16684": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Clinical Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Clinical Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Other Document: a summary of clinical supervision and training experience (as one complete document). Please Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Clinical Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by July 15, 2026. Applications received after July 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ The University of Rhode Island is seeking an a Clinical Assistant Professor of Clinical Practice to support a new Master’s program in Mental and Behavioral Health Counseling (https://web.uri.edu/psychology/academics/ms-in-mbhc?) The clinical faculty appointment to begin Summer 2026. Position Summary: The successful candidate will contribute to both the Master’s in Mental and Behavioral Health Counseling, as well as the Doctoral program in Clinical Psychology through teaching, leadership, and service to the university and community. Candidates should be able to demonstrate a strong commitment to clinical supervision and training, as well as mentorship and teaching at the graduate level. Candidates will work closely with the Director of the Psychological Consultation Center – the Psychology department’s community-based training clinic – as well as with department leadership. Key Duties and Responsibilities: ● Teach graduate-level courses to students in the Master’s program in Mental and Behavioral Health Counseling ( MBHC ) and the APA -accredited Ph.D. program in Clinical Psychology. Expectations are for teaching a total of 6 courses per year across the academic year and summer session. At least 2 of these courses must be practicum courses involving the training of clinical students. In additional, students will sign up for individual supervision. ● Supervise MBHC graduate students in clinical practice, including individual and group therapy work. ● Oversee and manage internship/externship placements for MBHC students. ● Contribute to the department’s mission of promoting diversity, equity, and inclusion in clinical research, teaching, and supervision. ● Mentor MBHC graduate and undergraduate students, fostering professional and academic growth. ● Engage in service to the department, college, and university through community outreach and advocacy events, committee participation, and other program development activities. ● Support administrative responsibilities in the Psychological Consultation Center. Qualifications Required: 1. Clinically-focused Masters or Doctorate degree (or a closely related field) at time of application. 2. Licensed or license-eligible as an LMHC or Psychologist in Rhode Island. 3. Experience in providing clinical supervision, with proficiency in empirically supported treatments (e.g., CBT , ACT , DBT , and/or other third-wave therapies). 4. Evidence of teaching excellence in core courses related to clinical psychology such as Psychopathology, Interventions or Service Ethics. 5. A strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in teaching, clinical practice, supervision, and service. 6. Demonstrated excellence in oral and written communication skills. Preferred: 1. Experience in teaching and supervising both individual and group therapy theory and practice. 2. Experience in clinical training with and professional mentorship of graduate students from diverse backgrounds. 3. Expertise in areas of clinical interest that complement departmental strengths (e.g., behavior change, substance use, trauma, child mental health, parenting, resilience in mental and behavioral health disorders). ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Non-tenure-track, Limited End Date of Restriction or Limitation Position is full-time calendar year, non-tenure-track, limited to 06/30/2028 with anticipated renewal. Department Information Department Psychology Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae. (#3) Other Document: a summary of clinical supervision and training experience (as one complete document). Please Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 107076 Posting Number F00512 Posting Date 01/21/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16117 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Clinically-focused Masters or Doctorate degree (or a closely related field) at time of application? Yes No * Are you licensed or license-eligible as an LMHC or Psychologist in Rhode Island? Yes No * Do you have experience in providing clinical supervision, with proficiency in empirically supported treatments (e.g., CBT, ACT, DBT, and/or other third-wave therapies)? Yes No * Do you have evidence of teaching excellence in core courses related to clinical psychology such as Psychopathology, Interventions or Service Ethics? Yes No * Do you have a strong commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion in teaching, clinical practice, supervision, and service? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17219": {
      "title": "Senior Higher Education Payroll Office Preaudit Clerk",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Senior Higher Education Payroll Office Preaudit Clerk Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Senior Higher Education Payroll Office Preaudit Clerk Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a full-time (35 hrs.), calendar year, permanent position. Generous benefits package including a tuition waiver for CCRI, RIC, and URI for the successful candidate, spouse, and dependents (if appliable) based on ESP-URI/NEA union guidelines. It also includes paid time off, paid state holidays, and a mandatory retirement plan in addition to many other types of benefits. To learn more about the benefit package, please visit www.exploreemployeebenefits.ri.gov The successful candidate will be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check paid by the University. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number CS02293 Job Title Senior Higher Education Payroll Office Preaudit Clerk Position Number 13408 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Pay Rate Salary Range $53,382 - $59,294 Pay Grade Level 319 Position Type Classified Civil Service Staff Union ESP-URI/NEARI (Educational Support Professionals) Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Restriction or Limitation Reason Funding End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Payroll Office Contact(s) Sean Nelson Talent Acquisition Specialist Human Resource Administration Contact Phone/Extension 401.874.5269 Contact Email sean.nelson@uri.edu Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Building(s) Carlotti Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Extension Contingency Notes Duties and Responsibilities ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLES OF WORK PERFORMED : -Within the college/university’s central payroll office, to process and perform preaudits on documents and/or computer files in connection with the college/university’s payrolls (State, student, temporary employees and/or instructional) received from the college/university’s various departments, State of Rhode Island’s Department of Administration’s Division of Human Resource and Office of Accounts and Control, and other federal and state agencies. -To analyze various payroll-related documents/reports prepared and/or approved by state and/or college/university human resources offices, reconcile any discrepancies to establish and maintain confidential employee payroll records received to determine their accuracy, legality, and compliance in accordance with the Council of Postsecondary Education, State of Rhode Island and the college/university’s policies and procedures. -To assist in the development, maintenance, and administration of payroll systems, policies, and procedures and to prepare related reconciliations, reports, statements, and analysis. -To review approved personnel action forms and determine the appropriate process to be completed, or determine any information needed to be able to complete. For required adjustments, calculate retroactive payment, and subsequently audit payroll vouchers to determine accuracy and ensure associated payments and deductions are made as authorized from start to completion for all actions. -To check payroll data for legality, accuracy and propriety to contractual agreements, rules and policies established by the State of Rhode Island and/or the college/university prior to posting payroll. -To establish, track, and maintain employees’ leave balances, including sick, vacation, personal, compensatory time. -To review and analyze accrual changes and process adjustments and discharges, including leave requests or termination balances, when applicable. -To prepare and maintain employee payroll records to ensure information is updated and accurate accordingly to all policies, contracts, and employee classification. -To utilize computer hardware to update and/or maintain state and college/university payroll data for payroll processing. -To correct erroneous payroll payments and update computer files with such corrections accordingly to policies. -To calculate and deposit on a timely basis employment and withholding taxes related to the college/university payrolls. -To assist in the preparation and issuance of calendar year-end wage and tax statements (W2s) for college/university payrolls. -To calculate corrections to wage and tax statements (W2s), and request copies from the state as needed. -To post employee time sheets, onto designated records/mainframe systems, obtain proper approvals and adherence to established college, State and Federal policies and procedures. -To prepare salary data reports for verification of employment forms sent from mortgage companies, banks, and attorneys; prepare reports for salary information requests from various federal and state agencies (e.g., labor and training, social security, state courts). -To calculate and prepare check change forms for return of salary overpayments to correct cash with state, internal account information, and individual year-to-date records. -To calculate and process retroactive adjustments to distribution of salary and fringe charges to the college’s/university’s accounting system. -To review, document and remain current on changes in rules, policies and procedures and revise as necessary due to changes including but not limited to contractual changes, effective dates of raises and pay periods, retroactive payments as posted, changes in state pension plans, codes and retirement contributions, states of emergency declared by the governor, and wellness credits. As required, train, supervise and evaluate assigned support staff and/or students engaged in performing payroll functions, and related capacities and abilities. -To provide high level of service and/or assistance to all employees with various payroll-related questions and transactions. -To do related work as required. Required Qualifications KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS , AND CAPACITIES : A thorough knowledge of the principles, practices and techniques involved in the implementation and administration of a complex payroll system for an institution of higher education, and the ability to apply such in a payroll office operation engaged in the preparation, processing and administration of a variety of regular and special payrolls, special payroll reports, payroll-oriented forms, and other pertinent payroll data; a working knowledge of office practices, principles and techniques needed to evaluate the policies, procedures and forms of a complex payroll system and to recommend necessary initiatives and adjustments; a strong understanding of payroll laws, regulations, and compliance requirement; the ability to interpret and apply rules, regulations, policies and procedures related to payroll administration; strong interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills and the ability to prepare clear and concise oral and written reports and analysis; the ability to maintain a current working knowledge of the latest requirements and developments in processing payrolls and other related areas; the ability to determine the mathematical accuracy, legality and propriety of payroll payments; strong analytical and problem-solving skills required to meet deadlines; ability to multi-task, organize, track and prioritize projects while working in a fast paced and continuously changing environment; ability to handle and safeguard sensitive and confidential information; a familiarity with spreadsheets, databases, word processing computer software and related technology; the ability to establish and maintain effective and collaborative working relationships and professionalism with supervisors, the college/university departments and other state and private agencies and organizations and employees; the ability to train, supervise and evaluate assigned support staff and/or students engaged in performing payroll functions; and related capacities and abilities. EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE : Education: Graduation from high school, including or supplemented by courses in bookkeeping, accounting computing or related subjects; and Experience: A minimum of 2 years as payroll clerk or higher, employment with responsibility for the preparation and processing of the payroll in a small state agency or private business operation, or employment with responsibility for a specific payroll function or activity in a large state agency or private business operation. Or, any combination of education and experience that shall be substantially equivalent to the above education and experience. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Work Hours Monday through Friday – 8:30 AM to 4:00 PM Days off: Saturday & Sunday Posting Date 10/19/2026 Closing Date 10/28/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants This is a full-time (35 hrs.), calendar year, permanent position. Generous benefits package including a tuition waiver for CCRI , RIC , and URI for the successful candidate, spouse, and dependents (if appliable) based on ESP - URI / NEA union guidelines. It also includes paid time off, paid state holidays, and a mandatory retirement plan in addition to many other types of benefits. To learn more about the benefit package, please visit www.exploreemployeebenefits.ri.gov The successful candidate will be subject to a pre-employment criminal background check paid by the University. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16955 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you currently a State employee WITHIN ESP-URI/NEARI? Yes No Graduation from high school, including or supplemented by courses in bookkeeping, accounting computing, or related subjects Yes No A minimum of 2 years as payroll clerk or higher? Yes No Employment with responsibility for the preparation and processing of the payroll in a small state agency or private operation? Yes No Employment with responsibility for a specific payroll function or activity in a large state agency or private business operation? Yes No To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17176": {
      "title": "Manager, Agronomy/Greenhouses/East Farm",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Manager, Agronomy/Greenhouses/East Farm Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Manager, Agronomy/Greenhouses/East Farm Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02231 Job Title Manager, Agronomy/Greenhouses/East Farm Position Number 108805 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 11 Pay Grade Range Hiring Salary Range: $65,000 - $75,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Plant Sciences & Entomology Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes The position is full-time calendar year, limited to 09/30/2027 with anticipated renewal. __________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/24/2026. Applications received after 10/24/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION WILL BE IN- PERSON POSITION SUMMARY : Responsible for operational oversight and management of the URI Agronomy Farm, East Farm, Greenhouses, and the Botanical Garden. Work cooperatively with faculty, staff, students, volunteers and the public to enable use of these farms for research, teaching, public education and outreach. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Ensure that all equipment, facilities, fields, and grounds are in good condition consistent with established safety standards and with use of the farms and garden as sites for research, teaching, public education and outreach. Operate farm equipment (tractors, harvest equipment, mower, tiller, etc.). Undertake minor repair and annual maintenance of farm equipment, as needed, and ensure that major repairs are undertaken by appropriate service providers. Supervise Assistant Farm Managers (East Farm and Greenhouse) ensuring all facilities are maintained, research and teaching efforts are supported, and that assistant managers are trained and have the resources needed to do their jobs. Supervise and/or train students, staff, and volunteers assigned to perform tasks related to upkeep and maintenance of the farms and teaching garden. Develop and implement an annual operating plan for the farms and teaching garden, including a budget and justification to support financial investments needed for maintenance and operations. Maintain inventory and purchase supplies, parts, etc. necessary for building, equipment, and grounds maintenance. Collaborate with faculty and staff in the development of applications for external funding to ensure that requests for all farm-related equipment, supplies and human resources needed to conduct the project are included in the proposal budget. Maintain equipment for weather condition reporting and facilitate data collection and reporting. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Coordinate the movement and use of shared farm equipment among University farms to ensure efficient utilization of resources. Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, word processing, database management and spreadsheet software, farm tools and equipment. All certifications to comply with USDA and university regulations. Must have certification or demonstrable familiarity with GAP (Good Agricultural Practices) accreditation. Must have or be able to obtain a RI Pesticide Applicator’s License. Must have a valid driver’s license. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree. 2. Minimum five years of agriculture-related experience. 3. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. 4. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 5. Demonstrated supervisory experience. 6. Demonstrated farm experience, including operating farm equipment appropriate to small-scale crop production and research trials. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. Ability to lift 50 lbs. Preferred Qualifications Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is required to work outdoors, sometimes in inclement weather, operate large machinery, and apply pesticides to crops periodically. Posting Date 10/08/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17170 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No * Do you have a minimum five years of agriculture-related experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated farm experience, including operating farm equipment appropriate to small-scale crop production and research trials? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have ability to lift 50 lbs? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17011": {
      "title": "Project Director, URI Medical School",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Project Director, URI Medical School Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Project Director, URI Medical School Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02200 Job Title Project Director, URI Medical School Position Number TBD FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Salary Hiring Range: $170,000 - $190,000 Pay Grade Range Grade Level: 18 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Office of the President Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Position is a full-time calendar year, limited term for 3 years with possible extension. __________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ THIS POSITION IS IMMEDIATELY ELIGIBLE FOR A HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : The University of Rhode Island ( URI ) seeks a highly strategic, execution-focused leader to serve as Project Director, School of Medicine Implementation. This individual will lead the project to coordinate the launch of URI’s new School of Medicine—one of the most significant academic, healthcare, and economic initiatives in the state. Reporting initially to the President of the University, working closely with the University’s implementation consultant, the Provost, and partnering with the Founding Dean upon their appointment, the Project Director will be responsible for end-to-end execution of the medical school implementation strategy, ensuring alignment across governance, accreditation, operations, fundraising, facilities, and statewide partners. This role directs the coordination, integration, and execution of a complex, multi-year initiative targeting inaugural student matriculation in FY30. Duties and Responsibilities KEY RESPONSIBILITIES : ● Serve as the University’s primary liaison to the implementation consultant, coordinating work plans, deliverables, governance activities, and transition of implementation responsibilities to the University and Founding Dean. ● In collaboration with University leadership and upon appointment of the Founding Dean, steward the overall implementation of the URI School of Medicine, coordinating all aspects from planning through launch and early operations. ● Establish timelines, dependencies, and risk mitigation strategies to ensure successful delivery. ● Provide regular, data-driven progress reporting to senior leadership. ● Prepare executive briefings, reports, presentations, and decision-support materials for University leadership, the Board of Trustees, state officials, and other key stakeholders to support informed decision-making and project accountability. Develop and manage an integrated master implementation plan aligned to: ○ Leadership and accreditation ○ Finance and Facilities Funding and Resource Development ○ Communications and Public Affairs ○ Community Engagement ● Serve as the operational lead for the School of Medicine Steering Group, in support of the President, Provost, and senior leadership. ● Work with the Founding Dean to manage the LCME accreditation process. ● Support the onboarding of the Founding Dean (target mid FY27) and serve as an advisor to them. ● Partner with Government Relations and University leadership to coordinate legislative engagement, state agency partnerships, and implementation activities requiring state support. ● Coordinate with the URI Foundation to support execution of a major fundraising campaign (~$100M goal) to meet startup funding requirements. ● Work with Founding Dean to develop short- and long-term financial sustainability models, and track financial milestones critical to reporting deadlines, accreditation milestones, and launch readiness. ● Work with the Administration and Finance teams of the University to develop and implement a phased facilities strategy which includes: ○ Renovation of existing campus spaces in preparation for initial cohorts ○ Expansion to support enrollment growth ○ Planning for a future dedicated medical school facility Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree required. 2. 10–15+ years of experience leading complex, multi-stakeholder projects and initiatives. 3. Demonstrated experience in: Large-scale program or project management; Cross-functional leadership and execution; Working with executive leadership, governing bodies, and external entities such as local/state government, hospital systems and service providers. 4. Experience building and managing governance structures, steering committees, advisory groups, and executive reporting processes. 5. Experience developing and tracking implementation plans, milestones, key performance indicators, budgets, risk mitigation strategies, and organizational readiness measures. 6. Exceptional organizational change management and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build trust and consensus among internal and external constituencies. 7. Strong executive communication skills, including preparation of materials and presentations for governing boards, executive leadership teams, elected officials, donors, and community stakeholders. 8. Demonstrated commitment to collaboration, inclusion, and mission-driven leadership. Preferred Qualifications Preferred: 1. Advanced degree strongly preferred (e.g., MBA , MPA , MPH , EdD). 2. Experience in: Academic medicine, healthcare systems, or higher education; Launching new programs, organizations, or major initiatives; Accreditation processes or regulatory environments 3. Familiarity with: Clinical partnerships and clinical education models; Public-sector or state-funded initiatives. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 08/29/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16997 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17108": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Talent Development",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Talent Development Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Coordinator, Talent Development Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02219 Job Title Coordinator, Talent Development Position Number 109024 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 7 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Ranage: $47,768 - $54,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Talent Development Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/13/2026. Applications received after 10/13/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Develop and maintain collaborative relationships through appreciative advising. Assist the student in optimizing their educational experience, support retention, and progress towards on-time graduation. Provide academic advising on an individual and group basis for students in Talent Development. Ensure that Talent Development students’ progress toward graduation in a timely and systematic way. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Provide academic advisement for Talent Development students through appreciative advising. Conduct weekly individual and group meetings with Talent Development students. Conduct Progress Check Point evaluations with Talent Development students. Assist in the development/coordination of support services such as those that support transition, first-year experience, and retention. Maintain confidential records, reports, and documentation regarding Talent Development students. Maintain a network of contacts and resources. Develop and maintain a comprehensive knowledge of resources that support student success, such as financial aid. Develop and maintain a comprehensive understanding of University policies and procedures that support and assist in retaining students. Assist in the coordination and update the Talent Development History book. Represent Talent Development on various University committees. Participate in scholastic standing review as needed. Assist with parent and family engagement. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Assist with Social Media accounts, i.e., Facebook, Twitter, LinkedIn, YouTube, Instagram, and TikTok. Assist/market all of the program’s special events, such as seminars and conferences, as they relate to student leadership development and peer mentoring. Work evenings and weekends, when necessary. Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal and university-issued computers, printers, database management, and spreadsheet software. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree. 2. Minimum of three years of combined experience in two or more of the following: recruiting and/or advising in an academic program setting, coordinating programs, or working in a Title IV grant program. 3. Demonstrated school-based experience and/or community work experience. 4. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. 5. Demonstrated program planning experience. 6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 7. Demonstrated computer skills. 8. Willingness to travel. 9. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s Degree. 2. Demonstrated ability to work both independently and as part of a team. 3. Demonstrated bilingual proficiency (spoken and written). 4. Academic advising experience gained while pursuing a graduate program. 5. Academic advising experience, including experience obtained while enrolled in a graduate degree program. 6. Demonstrated collaborative work style. 7. Demonstrated ability to use Google Suite (or similar platform). 8. Demonstrated ability to use Brightspace (or similar platform), presentation technology and student records systems (preferably Peoplesoft). 9. Demonstrated experience with Starfish. 10. Demonstrated ability to use Microsoft 365. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 09/22/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17101 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of three years of combined experience in two or more of the following: recruiting and/or advising in an academic program setting, coordinating programs, or working in a Title IV grant program? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated school-based experience and/or community work experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated program planning experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated computer skills? Yes No * Do you have willingness to travel? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
