    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17222": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Industrial and Systems Engineering (Advanced Manufacturing Operations and Autonomous Systems)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Professor, Industrial and Systems Engineering (Advanced Manufacturing Operations and Autonomous Systems) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Professor, Industrial and Systems Engineering (Advanced Manufacturing Operations and Autonomous Systems) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 4 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae (#3) Other Document - A narrative (up to two pages) describing your research (as one complete document). (#4) Other Document - A narrative (up to two pages) describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor, Industrial and Systems Engineering (Advanced Manufacturing Operations and Autonomous Systems) Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by November 15, 2026. Applications received after November 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. _______________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Serve as a tenure-track faculty member in the Industrial and Systems Engineering ( ISE ) program of the Department of Mechanical, Industrial and Systems Engineering. Establish and sustain a nationally and internationally recognized research program in advanced manufacturing operations, autonomous systems, and cyber-physical and robotic systems; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in industrial and systems engineering; and contribute to service within the department, college, university, and profession. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Develop and lead an externally funded, nationally and internationally recognized research program in one or more of the following areas: manufacturing systems; advanced manufacturing operations; optimization; simulation; learning and planning under uncertainty; cyber-physical systems; autonomous and robotic systems; human-centered automation and workforce systems; human autonomy teaming and human-system integration; Internet of Things (IoT); and hardware-software integration. Pursue and secure sponsored research funding from federal, state, industry, and other sources; prepare and submit competitive proposals; and manage awarded projects in accordance with sponsor and University requirements. Disseminate research results through peer-reviewed publications, conference presentations, and other scholarly outlets, and become a recognized leader in the field. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in industrial and systems engineering, including existing courses in operations research, simulation, manufacturing and automation, data analytics, and systems engineering, as assigned by the Department Chair. Develop new courses and curricular materials in the candidate’s area of expertise that strengthen the ABET -accredited B.S. in ISE , the accelerated B.S. in ISE to M.S. in Systems Engineering, and the M.S. and Ph.D. programs. Recruit, advise, supervise, and mentor M.S. and Ph.D. students; serve on graduate thesis and dissertation committees; and advise undergraduate students. Foster a nurturing and inclusive learning environment for students, faculty, and staff in the classroom, the laboratory, and the department. Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service, including committee work, program assessment, and ABET accreditation activities. Collaborate with departmental colleagues in established research strengths (autonomous systems, cyber-physical security, Industry 4.0, manufacturing systems, machine learning, and human factors) and with existing laboratories in digital twins, undersea vehicle technologies, and voting systems. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Mentor undergraduate capstone design teams in yearlong projects funded and mentored by industry and government partners. Contribute to undergraduate minors in robotics, sustainability, and entrepreneurship as appropriate to the candidate’s expertise. Build and maintain partnerships with Rhode Island’s network of defense, marine, and advanced manufacturing firms to facilitate sponsored research, student placements, and access to testbeds. Participate in student recruitment, outreach, and departmental events as requested. Perform other duties as assigned by the Department Chair or the Dean of Engineering. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers, and standard office equipment; word processing, spreadsheet, and presentation software; scientific computing, optimization, simulation, data analytics, and machine learning software; laboratory, manufacturing, robotic, and cyber-physical testbed equipment appropriate to the research program. ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Work may involve engineering laboratories, manufacturing testbeds, and field settings in which standard safety practices apply. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. An earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Industrial Engineering, Systems Engineering, or a closely related field, conferred by the date of appointment. 2. Demonstrated record of, or potential for, scholarly achievement evidenced by publications, presentations, or awards in areas related to advanced manufacturing operations and/or autonomous systems. 3. Evidence of, or potential for, teaching excellence at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels in industrial and systems engineering topics. 4. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively. 5. Demonstrated proficiency in oral communication skills. 6. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. PREFERRED : 1. At least one degree (bachelor’s, master’s, or doctoral) in Industrial Engineering or Industrial and Systems Engineering. 2. Demonstrated track record in computational and/or experimental research in optimization, simulation, or learning and planning under uncertainty. 3. Ability to teach courses in at least one of the following subjects: operations research, simulation, manufacturing and automation, data analytics, or systems engineering, as well as the ability to develop new courses in their area of expertise. 4. Ability to foster a nurturing and inclusive learning environment for students, faculty, and staff. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Industrial & Systems Engr Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 4 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Curriculum Vitae (#3) Other Document – A narrative (up to two pages) describing your research (as one complete document). (#4) Other Document – A narrative (up to two pages) describing your teaching background and philosophy (as one complete document). Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 107576 Posting Number F00531 Posting Date 10/20/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17217 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Other Document Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have or will have an earned doctorate (Ph.D.) in Industrial Engineering, Systems Engineering, or a closely related field, conferred by the date of appointment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated record of, or potential for, scholarly achievement evidenced by publications, presentations, or awards in areas related to advanced manufacturing operations and/or autonomous systems? Yes No * Do you have evidence of, or potential for, teaching excellence at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels in industrial and systems engineering topics? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work collaboratively? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in oral communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
