    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17014": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Learning &amp; Development",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Assistant Director, Learning &amp; Development Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Assistant Director, Learning & Development Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02175 Job Title Assistant Director, Learning & Development Position Number Job code # (101927) FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level 12 Pay Grade Range $80,000 - $100,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Human Resources Contact(s) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary The search will remain open until the position has been filled. ________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : The Assistant Director, Learning & Development is responsible for designing, developing, and delivering talent development programs that strengthen leadership capability, support employee growth, and advance professional learning for faculty and staff. Reporting to the Director of Talent, this role partners with university leaders, Human Resources colleagues, and subject matter experts to implement the University’s talent development strategy by creating meaningful learning experiences that foster a culture of continuous learning and support the University’s mission, values, and strategic priorities. Serving as the functional lead for Workday Learning and related learning technologies, the Assistant Director of Learning & Development develops learning pathways, leadership and manager development programs, onboarding curriculum, and professional development opportunities. This role coordinates learning resources, supports communities of practice, evaluates learning outcomes, and helps build a sustainable learning ecosystem that enables faculty and staff to grow, contribute, and succeed throughout their careers at URI . Duties and Responsibilities Key Responsibilities: Learning Culture & Employee Development: Promote a culture of continuous learning by increasing awareness, participation, and engagement in professional development opportunities, learning resources, and career development initiatives. Onboarding & Learning Integration: Partner with the Talent Engagement team to develop onboarding curriculum, new supervisor learning, orientation resources, and learning pathways that support successful employee transitions and long-term success. Compliance & Required Learning: Coordinate required learning initiatives by partnering with content owners across the University to administer, assign, track, and report on compliance-related training and required learning. Leadership & Manager Development: Design, coordinate, and facilitate leadership and manager development programs that strengthen supervisory effectiveness, coaching, communication, performance management, employee development, and leadership capability. Professional Learning Programs: Develop and manage professional development programs, learning pathways, workshops, learning series, and development opportunities that support career growth and continuous learning across the University. Communities of Practice: Establish and support communities of practice that encourage collaboration, knowledge sharing, innovation, and continuous professional learning among faculty and staff. Learning Technology Administration: Serve as the functional administrator for Workday Learning and related learning technologies, including learning assignments, course administration, governance, reporting, user support, and administration of LinkedIn Learning. Learning Analytics & Continuous Improvement: Evaluate learning effectiveness through participation data, learning analytics, stakeholder feedback, and assessment outcomes to continuously improve learning programs and employee development initiatives. University Partnership & Consultation: Partner with academic and administrative leaders to assess learning needs, identify capability gaps, and recommend learning solutions that support departmental priorities and institutional goals. Learning Experience Design: Design, develop, and coordinate learning experiences by partnering with subject matter experts, external facilitators, digital learning platforms, and instructional design resources to deliver engaging, scalable, and impactful development opportunities. SKILLS & COMPETENCIES : • Learning Program Design : Ability to design and implement learning programs, development pathways, and learning experiences that support employee growth and organizational capability. • Leadership Development: Ability to develop and coordinate programs that strengthen leadership effectiveness, supervisory skills, coaching, and employee development. • Adult Learning Principles: Knowledge of adult learning theory and the ability to create engaging and meaningful learning experiences. • Learning Culture Development : Ability to foster a culture of continuous learning through communication, engagement strategies, and development opportunities. • Learning Technology Management: Ability to administer and optimize learning management systems, Workday Learning, LinkedIn Learning, and related technologies. • Facilitation & Presentation Skills: Ability to facilitate workshops, development sessions, communities of practice, and learning events with confidence and professionalism. • Stakeholder Partnership: Ability to build collaborative relationships and influence outcomes across academic and administrative units. • Project Management: Ability to manage multiple learning initiatives, priorities, and timelines while ensuring successful execution. • Data Analysis & Program Evaluation: Ability to analyze participation, engagement, and effectiveness data to assess learning outcomes and drive improvement. • Communication Skills: Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to translate complex concepts into practical learning solutions. • Adaptability & Innovation: Ability to identify emerging learning needs and develop creative approaches to employee development. • Compliance & Governance Awareness : Understanding of learning governance, compliance training requirements, and administrative processes related to employee development. Required Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree required. • Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in learning and development, talent development, organizational development, training, human resources, higher education administration, or a related field. • Experience designing and implementing employee development programs. • Experience facilitating training, workshops, or development programs. • Experience working with learning management systems or learning technologies. Preferred Qualifications • Master’s degree in Human Resources, Organizational Development, Adult Learning, Higher Education Administration, Instructional Design, or a related field. • Experience in higher education or another complex organization. • Experience with Workday Learning or similar learning management systems. • Experience supporting leadership development and manager effectiveness programs. • Professional certifications such as SHRM , ATD , CPTD , or related credentials. Environmental Conditions Posting Date 07/10/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/16827 Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in learning and development, talent development, organizational development, training, human resources, higher education administration, or a related field? yes no * Do you have experience designing and implementing employee development programs? yes no * Do you have experience facilitating training, workshops, or development programs? yes no * Do you have experience working with learning management systems or learning technologies? yes no To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17116": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Program Development, Assessment &amp; Data Analytics",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Program Development, Assessment &amp; Data Analytics Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Coordinator, Program Development, Assessment & Data Analytics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02214 Job Title Coordinator, Program Development, Assessment & Data Analytics Position Number 109286 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 10 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $65,000 - $75,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department COEDU Dean's Office Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 10/03/2026. Applications received after 10/03/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ POSITION SUMMARY : Provide coordination for program development, assessment, accreditation, compliance, and data analytics for the Feinstein College of Education. Support the Dean, Associate Deans, Assistant Dean, program faculty, and staff in the development, revision, evaluation, and continuous improvement of academic programs, including educator preparation programs subject to Rhode Island Department of Education approval and national accreditation standards. Coordinate College-level data collection, assessment planning, reporting, and analysis to support program quality, state approval, national accreditation, strategic planning, enrollment management, and continuous improvement. Serve as a key liaison between the College, University offices, the Rhode Island Department of Education, national accreditation bodies, and other external partners related to program approval, assessment, compliance, and reporting. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : ● Coordinate and support College-level assessment, accreditation, and compliance activities for educator preparation and related academic programs. ● Support the College’s work with the Rhode Island Department of Education, including program approval, regulatory reporting, data submissions, site visits, evidence collection, and responses to state requests. ● Coordinate national accreditation activities for the College, including maintaining evidence systems, tracking standards, preparing reports, supporting site visits, and working with faculty and staff to ensure timely completion of accreditation requirements. ● Work closely with the Dean, Associate Deans, Assistant Dean, program directors, faculty, and staff to support the development, revision, and evaluation of academic programs, new tracks, certificates, and other programmatic initiatives. ● Maintain and improve systems for collecting, organizing, analyzing, and reporting assessment data across College programs. ● Coordinate data collection from internal and external sources, including student enrollment, retention, completion, licensure, clinical placement, graduate outcomes, employer feedback, candidate performance, and other program quality indicators. ● Analyze and summarize data to support College decision-making, continuous improvement, accreditation, state approval, strategic planning, and program review. ● Prepare reports, dashboards, summaries, and presentations for internal and external audiences, including College leadership, faculty committees, University offices, state agencies, and accreditation reviewers. ● Support faculty and program staff in developing and implementing assessment plans, rubrics, surveys, data collection tools, and continuous improvement processes. ● Coordinate communication and documentation related to curriculum changes, program approvals, assessment timelines, accreditation requirements, and compliance deadlines. ● Maintain accurate records and databases related to program assessment, accreditation evidence, state approval documentation, curriculum revisions, and required reporting. ● Monitor changes in state and national standards related to educator preparation, accreditation, licensure, and program approval, and communicate relevant updates to College leadership and program faculty. ● Support the College’s program review and continuous improvement processes by identifying trends, gaps, risks, and opportunities based on available data. ● Assist with special projects related to program development, enrollment planning, grants, strategic initiatives, and external reporting as assigned. ● Represent the College on University committees, working groups, and external meetings related to assessment, accreditation, data, program approval, and educator preparation. ● Provide Brightspace support for faculty and staff. ● Support course level assessment implementation & ensure alignment with accreditation expectations. ● Provide administrative and technical support in instructional design and curriculum development to ensure assessment elements are embedded in all activities to support the College mission for all degree programs. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computer; Microsoft Office; Google Workspace; spreadsheet and database software; survey and assessment platforms; reporting and dashboard tools; student information systems; accreditation or evidence-management systems; and other University systems as required. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in education, higher education, public administration, data analytics, assessment, program evaluation, or a related field. 2. Minimum of three years of experience in assessment, accreditation, program evaluation, data reporting, compliance, institutional research, or academic program administration. 3. Experience collecting, managing, analyzing, and reporting data. 4. Experience preparing written reports, summaries, presentations, or documentation for internal or external review. 5. Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects, timelines, documentation, and reporting requirements. 6. Demonstrated experience representing an organization in various working groups 7. Demonstrated attention to detail and accuracy. 8. Demonstrated ability to interpret policies, standards, regulations, or reporting requirements. 9. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. 10. Demonstrated interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners. 11. Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team. 12. Demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, spreadsheets, databases, and/or data management systems. 13. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups and populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Master’s degree in education, higher education, public administration, data analytics, assessment, program evaluation, or a related field. 2. Experience with educator preparation programs. 3. Experience with Rhode Island Department of Education program approval, educator certification, or related state reporting requirements. 4. Experience with national accreditation processes in education, such as AAQEP or similar accrediting bodies. 5. Experience working in higher education. 6. Experience with data visualization, dashboards, or reporting tools. 7. Experience with statistical software, survey tools, assessment platforms, or student information systems. 8. Experience supporting curriculum development, academic program review, or new program approval processes. 9. Knowledge of educator licensure, clinical placements, candidate assessment, or program completed outcomes. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 09/18/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17070 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in education, higher education, public administration, data analytics, assessment, program evaluation, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have minimum of three years of experience in assessment, accreditation, program evaluation, data reporting, compliance, institutional research, or academic program administration? Yes No * Do you have experience collecting, managing, analyzing, and reporting data? Yes No * Do you have experience preparing written reports, summaries, presentations, or documentation for internal or external review? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to manage complex projects, timelines, documentation, and reporting requirements? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience representing an organization in various working groups? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated attention to detail and accuracy? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to interpret policies, standards, regulations, or reporting requirements? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated interpersonal skills and ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, administrators, and external partners? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency with Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, spreadsheets, databases, and/or data management systems? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups and populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
