    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17240": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Inner Space Center (ISC) &amp; Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Coordinator, Inner Space Center (ISC) &amp; Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Coordinator, Inner Space Center (ISC) & Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02242 Job Title Coordinator, Inner Space Center (ISC) & Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute Position Number PS# 00008223 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 9 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $77,000 - $82,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department GSO Research Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Narragansett Bay Campus Grant Funded Yes Extension Contingency Notes The position is full-time calendar year, limited to 06/27/2027 with anticipated renewal. __________________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/05/2026. Applications received after 11/05/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION IS ELIGIBLE FOR A REMOTE / HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : Assist the Inner Space Center and Ocean Exploration Cooperative Institute ( OECI ) with programmatic and administrative support. Develop and implement protocols to track spending across all ISC projects. Coordinate financial and administrative support for all ISC transactions and serve as a liaison with URI Office of Sponsored Projects, and the URI OECI administrative office. Assist with pre and post award requirements in coordination with URI OSP . Assist with managing the ISC calendar of meetings to include scheduling and keeping meeting minutes for routine meetings with funding agencies. Hire contractors and students working on projects and general administrative tasks. Assist with travel, procurement, and invoicing functions within the ISC . Track the ISC Service Center budget and provide regular reports. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Track and report financial and progress across ISC projects to include financial and operational milestones. Assist in invoicing and financial reporting for each project. Develop protocols to track operational milestones and spending across all ISC projects. Manage the finances and administration of several multi-year government funded projects. This includes processing and managing sub awards (payments, budget, and close-out); developing annual budgets; processing and managing awards(including expense monitoring) through URI systems. Submit and track award actions through the URI system to ensure timely processing. Process monthly invoices and clearing of advances. Prepare monthly financial reports for multiple projects. Review, interpret and analyze monthly spending and compare against budgets. Prepare quarterly accruals, end of year and end of project financial reports to sponsors. Assist in the preparation of budgets and supporting documents for proposals and related submission. Manage travel for ISC . Prepare and assist in all phases of domestic and international travel as needed. Coordinate all related logistics, including, but not limited to: lodging, meals, ground transport and daily logistical schedules, etc. Initiate Travel Authorization Requests (pre-travel) and submit Expense Reports (post travel) for ISC staff, contractors, and students. Assist in human resources actions including participation in ISC search committees (including required trainings) as requested; assisting in advertising, hiring of URI and non- URI project staff; mentoring/orienting administrative and finance staff; hiring and supervising students; processing Graduate Assistantships; processing faculty and internal payroll contracts; processing and managing personal service contract. Assist with ISC interns. Coordinate logistics for meetings and tours at URI and as necessary for ISC projects. This includes obtaining visas, pre-departure and arrival orientations, lodging, transport, health and accident insurance and ground transport. Manage ISC’S Service Center and project purchasing and procurement of supplies and equipment. Responsible for coordinating quotes, RFQ’s, RFP’s, working with suppliers, etc. Coordinate ISC space, building maintenance and repair. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Travel one or two times a year to partner institutions or NOAA offices to review finances, standard operating procedures, administrative policy, and systems, and participate in work planning. Train URI and non- URI project staff on protocols, review of policy and procedures, etc. Initiate and prepare personnel action forms. Perform additional duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers; Google Workspace, Microsoft 365, Adobe Acrobat. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree. 2. Minimum three years of business management experience. 3. Demonstrated experience with project and personnel management. 4. Demonstrated experience in budget preparation and income/expense analysis. 5. Demonstrated ability to work in a fast-paced and deadline-driven environment. 6. Demonstrated experience with Google Workspace suite of tools. 7. Demonstrated experience with web-based reporting and management. 8. Demonstrated ability to prepare and present reports. 9. Demonstrated organizational skills. 10. Demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. 11. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 12. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Minimum three years of business management experience in a research setting at a university, college, or government agency. 2. Demonstrated knowledge of federal grants management, specifically the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17223 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree? Yes No * Do you have a minimum three years of business management experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with project and personnel management? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in budget preparation and income/expense analysis? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work in a fast-paced and deadline-driven environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with Google Workspace suite of tools? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience with web-based reporting and management? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to prepare and present reports? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated organizational skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
