    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17228": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant I, Facilities Group",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Executive Assistant I, Facilities Group Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Executive Assistant I, Facilities Group Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02243 Job Title Executive Assistant I, Facilities Group Position Number 107574 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 7 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $60,000 - $65,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Facilities Services Admin. Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/14/2026. Applications received after 11/14/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION SCHEDULE WILL BE IN- PERSON . POSITION SUMMARY : Serve as executive assistant to the Associate Vice President of Facilities, providing critical administrative support and executive coordination, such as planning and managing the AVP’s schedule and appearances, planning and hosting events, arranging meetings, handling confidential and sensitive materials and information, and facilitating interactions between the AVP and internal and external stakeholders. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Assist the AVP in carrying out administrative responsibilities; research and troubleshoot issues needing resolution at the department level. Provide confidential administrative services, including but not limited to: arranging meetings; typing reports, correspondence, speeches and related materials; making travel arrangements; drafting and responding to routine correspondence; preparing and maintaining spreadsheets; keeping department websites updated. Develop and prepare presentations, speeches, and related materials to support the AVP and departmental initiatives. Plan, arrange, schedule, and conduct special events, such as meetings, conferences, and other events. Support marketing and outreach efforts as necessary. Coordinate committee meetings, including scheduling, preparing agendas/meeting materials, recording and distributing meeting notes, and managing follow-ups. Manage calendars and coordinate travel arrangements for the AVP and Facilities Group senior leadership. Answer phones, greet visitors, and provide information to a diverse constituency. Exhibiting a high degree of tact and sensitivity, deal directly with the public, students, faculty, staff, and officials (both within and outside the university) on behalf of the AVP . Prioritize responses to correspondence, phone calls, and various issues, minimizing demands on the AVP , allowing him/her to focus on broader and more critical issues. Receive, prioritize, track, and process responses to administrative requests to ensure timely responses and appropriate follow-ups. In consultation with the AVP , assist in the preparation and administration of the department’s budget(s). Develop and maintain office files and budget records, and ensure their confidentiality Assist the AVP with budget monitoring and tracking to ensure expenses remain within approved departmental budgets. Provide administrative support for confidential real estate transactions, demonstrating discretion and confidentiality of sensitive information and documentation. Prepare, coordinate, process, and assist with human resources documentation, including Employee Action Forms (EAFs) and Personnel Action Forms (PAFs), ensuring accuracy, confidentiality, and timely submission. Interview and recommend support staff and student help for appointment. Train, schedule, and assign workloads to support staff and student help. Develop and maintain a signature tracking system to monitor documents requiring the AVP’s review, approval, or signature, ensuring timely completion and processing. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Work on special projects as assigned by the AVP . Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers; word processing, spreadsheet, database management, and scheduling software; PeopleSoft; video conferencing, fax and copying machines; AI assistants; calculator. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. High school diploma. 2. Minimum three years of progressively responsible experience in the capacity of administrative support in a complex professional environment;. 3. Demonstrated time management and organizational skills. 4. Demonstrated ability to prioritize in a fast-paced environment (i.e., prioritizing efforts and advancing multiple ongoing projects/efforts). 5. Demonstrated proficiency with word processing, spreadsheet, database, and scheduling software. 6. Demonstrated interpersonal and written and verbal communication skills. 7. Demonstrated experience in the organization, coordination, and supervision of support staff. 8. Demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality. 9. Demonstrated ability to work in a culturally diverse environment. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Associate’s or Bachelor’s Degree. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : The incumbent is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/21/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17224 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma? Yes No * Do you have a minimum three years of progressively responsible experience in the capacity of administrative support in a complex professional environment? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated time management and organizational skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to prioritize in a fast-paced environment (i.e., prioritizing efforts and advancing multiple ongoing projects/efforts)? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency with word processing, spreadsheet, database, and scheduling software? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated interpersonal and written and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in the organization, coordination, and supervision of support staff? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to maintain confidentiality? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work in a culturally diverse environment? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
