    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17241": {
      "title": "Manager, Projects I (Small Projects)",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Manager, Projects I (Small Projects) Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Manager, Projects I (Small Projects) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02244 Job Title Manager, Projects I (Small Projects) Position Number Job code # (100657) FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union PSA/NEA - Professional Staff Assoc Pay Grade Level Grade Level: 12 Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $80,000 - $86,000 Status Calendar Year, Full-time, Permanent Department Information Department Capital Program Design & Delivery - Small Projects Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by 11/12/2026. Applications received after 11/12/2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION IS ELIGIBLE FOR A HYBRID WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : Provide project management services to the University community for construction, renovation and deferred maintenance projects. Provide technical and management assistance to URI’s Office of Capital Program Design & Delivery – Small Projects to coordinate with Campus Design, Capital Construction, Planning & Real Estate Development and Facilities Operations. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Manage and coordinate URI personnel to develop design and spatial, physical efficiencies within existing building systems. Coordinate work with consultants and contractors for small projects. Develop programs and work with committees to achieve the Capital Program Design & Delivery – Small Projects’ goals and requirements. Manage, inspect and document construction, renovation and deferred maintenance projects. Manage design and construction contracts. Conduct field inspections and surveys of campus grounds to document existing conditions. Determine necessary repairs and upgrades for efficient and reliable use and operations. Develop and complete budgets, schedules, permits and reports as required. Perform regulatory review and research to determine requirements and to insure University compliance. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Perform other duties as required or assigned. LICENSES , TOOLS AND EQUIPMENT : Personal computers, printers; word processing, spreadsheet and database software. Valid driver’s license. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Bachelor’s degree in architecture, civil or mechanical engineering or a related field. 2. Minimum of five years of cumulative experience in design, project management, and construction administration. 3. Demonstrated working knowledge of building code requirements and standard construction details; Demonstrated organizational and time management skills. 4. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 5. Demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills. 6. Demonstrated experience in developing and analyzing data and writing reports. 7. Demonstrated supervisory experience. 8. Demonstrated working knowledge of AutoCAD. 9. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Demonstrated design experience in multiple types of buildings. 2. Demonstrated experience in A/E office. 3. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff and contractors. 4. Demonstrated computer skills (including, MS Word, EXCEL , PowerPoint, Access and MS Projects.) ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is subject to both inside and outside work and extreme cold and hot temperatures can be encountered. The potential exists where noise, vibration, hazards, atmospheric conditions, oils and wearing a respirator might also be encountered. This position involves traveling throughout the University and could on occasion require bending, reaching, ascending and descending ladders and stairs, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, standing, walking, pushing, pulling, lifting, feeling, talking, and hearing. This position requires 24-hour call back in cases of emergency and supervisory presence, when required, on all shifts. Posting Date 10/23/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17237 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a Bachelor’s degree in architecture, civil or mechanical engineering or a related field? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of five years of cumulative experience in design, project management, and construction administration? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated working knowledge of building code requirements and standard construction details; Demonstrated organizational and time management skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated strong interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in developing and analyzing data and writing reports? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated supervisory experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated working knowledge of AutoCAD? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Are you a URI employee currently in a position covered by the PSA Union? (You will not be disqualified for answering \"No\") Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17255": {
      "title": "Head Coach, Club Crew Team",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | Head Coach, Club Crew Team Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm Head Coach, Club Crew Team Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 3 (PDF) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document - US Rowing Level 1 (or Higher) Coach Certification. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SF02245 Job Title Head Coach, Club Crew Team Position Number 109247 FTE 1.00 FLSA Exempt Position Type Professional Staff Union Non-Union Non-Classified Staff Pay Grade Level Grade Level: N/A Pay Grade Range Salary Hiring Range: $50,000 - $55,000 Status Academic Year, Full-time, Limited Department Information Department Campus Recreation Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Phone/Extension Contact Email Physical Demands Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingency Notes Position is full-time, academic year, limited to 06/26/2027 with anticipated renewal. _______________________________________________________________________________________ Job Description Summary Search will be open until filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by November 10, 2026. Applications received after November 10, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION WILL BE AN IN- PERSON WORK SCHEDULE . POSITION SUMMARY : Plan, organize, and direct all aspects of a highly competitive collegiate rowing program, ensuring strong team development and operational excellence. Duties and Responsibilities KEY DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Promote fair play and good sportsmanship at all practices and competitions. Uphold, enforce, and adhere to all URI policies and procedures. Adhere to and enforce safety guidelines for on-water sessions. Attend and coordinate all team practices. Accompany team to all regattas during the fall and spring racing seasons. Schedule and coordinate all team-related events including practice, team meetings, workouts, and regatta participation. Coordinate team travel in cooperation with the Assistant Director, Competitive Sports, and the team’s executive board. Oversee the recruitment process of prospective student athletes. Remain abreast of and adhere to all US Rowing, ACRA , and other relevant rules and regulations. Maintain office hours and availability to meet with athletes during the academic year. Oversee the development of the team’s annual budget and management of team finances in cooperation with the team’s executive board and the Assistant Director, Competitive Sports. Liaise with the Old and Ancient Rowers Society of Rhode Island ( OARS ) on all matters relating to the Flagg Rowing Center. Oversee the rigging and maintenance of the team’s fleet and other equipment. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES : Attend select University functions as directed by the Assistant Director, Competitive Sports. Assist with fundraising and alumni engagement activities, in cooperation with the team’s executive board, the URI Foundation, and the Assistant Director, Competitive Sports. Work a Flexible schedule including some nights and weekends. Perform other duties as required. LICENSES , TOOLS , AND EQUIPMENT : Proficiency with personal computers, printers, word‑processing, database management, and spreadsheet software; Current USRowing Level 1 Coach Certification; Current Rhode Island Boating Safety Certification or obtain within the first 30 days of employment; Current CPR , first aid and Automatic External Defibrillator ( AED ) Certifications or obtain within the first 30 days of employment; Current US Center for SafeSport Certification or obtain within the first 30 days of employment. Required Qualifications QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Current USRowing Level 1 Coach Certification or higher. 2. Minimum of two years of rowing coaching experience. 3. Demonstrated experience in boat repair and maintenance. 4. Demonstrated ability to work with college students, alumni, staff, and donors. 5. Demonstrated proficiency in interpersonal and verbal communication skills. 6. Demonstrated proficiency with written communication skills. 7. Demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations. 8. Willingness to work evenings and weekends. 9. Willingness to travel locally, regionally, and nationally. 10. Current US Center for SafeSport Certification or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment. 11. Current Rhode Island Boating Safety Certification or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment. 12. Current CPR , first aid and Automatic External Defibrillator ( AED ) Certifications or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications PREFERRED : 1. Bachelor’s Degree. 2. Demonstrated evidence of USRowing Level 2 Coach Certification or higher. 3. Minimum of one year of rowing coaching experience in a collegiate or university setting. 4. Demonstrated experience in planning and supporting fundraising initiatives. 5. Demonstrated experience with fundraising initiatives. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Environmental Conditions ENVIRONMENTAL CONDITIONS : This position is not substantially exposed to adverse environmental conditions. Posting Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 3 ( PDF ) documents to your online Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter. (#2) Resume. (#3) Other Document – US Rowing Level 1 (or Higher) Coach Certification. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17245 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Resume Other Document Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a current USRowing Level 1 Coach Certification or higher? Yes No * Do you have a minimum of two years of rowing coaching experience? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated experience in boat repair and maintenance? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with college students, alumni, staff, and donors? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency in interpersonal and verbal communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated proficiency with written communication skills? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated ability to work with diverse groups/populations? Yes No * Do you have willingness to work evenings and weekends? Yes No * Do you have willingness to travel locally, regionally, and nationally? Yes No * Do you have current US Center for SafeSport Certification or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment? Yes No * Do you have current Rhode Island Boating Safety Certification or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment? Yes No * Do you have current CPR, first aid and Automatic External Defibrillator (AED) Certifications or ability to obtain within the first 30 days of employment? Yes No How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
