    "https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17256": {
      "title": "ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC EDUCATION",
      "description": "University Of Rhode Island Applicant Portal | ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC EDUCATION Skip to Main Content University Of Rhode Island H uman R esource A dministration 80 Lower College Road, Kingston, RI 02881 urihr@ucs.uri.edu - 401.874.2416 - 401.874.5741 (fax) URI Homepage Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help About URI Office of Human Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Campus Maps & Directions Hours: Monday - Friday 8.30am to 4.30pm ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC EDUCATION Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please attach the following 2 (PDF) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter (maximum length 2 pages). (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Details Position Information Job Title ASSISTANT PROFESSOR OF MUSIC EDUCATION Job Description Summary, Duties and Responsibilities, Required Qualifications and Preferred Qualifications The search will remain open until the position has been filled. First consideration will be given to applications received by Dec. 15, 2026. Applications received after Dec. 15, 2026 may be reviewed depending on search progress and needs but are not guaranteed full consideration. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ About URI : The University of Rhode Island enrolls approximately 17,000 students across its graduate and undergraduate programs and is the State’s flagship public research university, as well as the land grant and sea grant university, for the state of Rhode Island. The main campus is located in the historic village of Kingston, and the Bay Campus is located in Narragansett. Both campuses are near major beaches in a beautiful coastal community. URI is just 30 minutes from Providence, RI and within easy reach of Newport, Boston, and New York City. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ THE POSITION WILL BE IN- PERSON . This position is in the Department of Music in the College of Arts and Sciences. The Music Department is located within the newly renovated URI Fine Arts Center, which houses the Music, Theater, and Art departments. Learn about the URI Music Department at: https://web.uri.edu/music/ POSITION SUMMARY : The Department of Music at the University of Rhode Island invites applications for an Assistant Professor of Music Education, a full-time tenure-track appointment beginning in the 2027-2028 academic year, starting July 1, 2027. KEY RESPONSIBILITIES : Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in music education, with an emphasis in primary or secondary education, as well as teaching other courses to be determined by departmental needs and applicant’s qualifications. This faculty member will maintain an active research/creative activity agenda. This faculty member will also serve as the department’s liaison to the College of Education and will participate in departmental committees and events. DUTIES : ● Serve as Director of Music Education; in conjunction with the College of Education, coordinate curriculum alignment, certification requirements, assessment practices and field placements for practicums. ● Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in music education. ● Develop and maintain an active research/creative activity agenda. ● Teaching other courses to be determined by departmental needs and/or applicant’s qualifications. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ QUALIFICATIONS REQUIRED : 1. Terminal degree in music (PhD, EdD, or DMA ) or ABD status. 2. Minimum record of three years of successful teaching experience at the primary or secondary level in public schools or equivalent. 3. Demonstrated potential for research and/or creative activities appropriate to the field. 4. Experience with use of technology in the music education classroom. PREFERRED : 1. Record of success teaching music education at the collegiate level. 2. Ability to cultivate and maintain relationships with regional music educators. 3. Strong communication and interpersonal skills with flexible attitude and ability to work collaboratively. 4. Experience with and expertise in teaching music production and music technologies in the primary or secondary classroom setting. 5. Ability to teach other courses depending on the applicant’s qualifications and departmental needs. ________________________________________________________________________________________________________ EEO Statement: URI is unwavering in its commitment to equal opportunity, community, equity, and diversity. In furtherance of its mission to serve and support all learners as the state’s public flagship university, URI continues to expand efforts to recruit and retain a broadly representative workforce as well as to regularly evaluate the effectiveness of those efforts. All employment decisions, including hiring, are made without regard to protected status. Qualified individuals with disabilities may request reasonable accommodation by contacting the URI benefits office at 401-874-2416. For TTY assistance, contact R.I. Relay Services at 711. Union AAUP - American Assoc of Univ Professors Status Academic Year, Full-time, Tenure-track, Permanent End Date of Restriction or Limitation Department Information Department Music Contact(s) Please note: Job applications must be submitted directly online only at: (https://jobs.uri.edu) Contact Email Campus Location Kingston Grant Funded No Extension Contingent on Funding Date Special Instructions to Applicants Please attach the following 2 ( PDF ) documents to your online Faculty Employment Application: (#1) Cover letter (maximum length 2 pages). (#2) Curriculum Vitae. Note: References will be upon request by the search committee. Posting Information Position Number 106686 Posting Number F00533 Posting Date 10/27/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Quicklink for Posting https://jobs.uri.edu/postings/17252 Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a terminal degree in music (PhD, EdD, or DMA) or ABD status? Yes No * Do you have a minimum record of three years of successful teaching experience at the primary or secondary level in public schools or equivalent? Yes No * Do you have demonstrated potential for research and/or creative activities appropriate to the field? Yes No * Do you have experience with use of technology in the music education classroom? Yes No * How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Chronicle Academic Careers Higher Ed Jobs Indeed Inside Higher Ed New England Herc The Edu Ledger LinkedIn Asiana In Higher Ed Disable in High ed Blacks In Higher Ed Diversity Jobs HBCU Connect Hispanic in Higher ed LGBT in Higher Ed Native American in Higher ed Woman and Higher Ed Veterans in Higher Edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
